const PEOPLE_TOOLS = [
  { tool: 'GetRequestedClosedCases', purpose: 'Retrieve a report of requested and closed cases.' },
  { tool: 'OverAllStatusCases', purpose: 'Retrieve the overall status for all cases. In the payload, set method=\'allReportColumn\', repType=\'adminReports\', and needAgentList=false. Here duration can have 5 values 1,2,3,4,5. 1 is for last 24 hours, 2 is for last 48 hours, 3 is past week, 4 is for last month and 5 is for last 3 months. If duration is not mentioned then it will be considered as 3.' },
  { tool: 'addAdminBeneficiary', purpose: 'This action is used by an admin to add a beneficiary to an enrollment.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollments' },
  { tool: 'addAdminEnrollment', purpose: 'This action is used by an admin to enroll a user in a benefit plan.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'addAndTagUserKra', purpose: 'Creates a new KRA and tags it to a specific employee in one step. Requires kra_name (mandatory, max 500 chars). Optional: description (max 5000 chars), weightage (float), include_in_library (true/false to also add to org KRA library). The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'addCandidate', purpose: 'Adds a new candidate to the onboarding module. first_name (text), last_name (text), and mail (email) are mandatory - if any are missing from the user\'s request, ask for them once in a single question before invoking this tool. Do not invoke without all three. Before invoking, also ask in the same question: \'Should I trigger onboarding?\' and \'Should I initiate associated workflows?\'. Store the user\'s answers. After a successful add: if the user agreed to trigger onboarding, call triggerCandidateOnboarding with the returned candidateId (and formId from listOnboardingRecords); if the user agreed to initiate workflows, call triggerWorkflow with the returned candidateId. Each is called independently based on the user\'s answers. Optional: id (external employee ID, text), location_id (long, resolve via getLocationDetails - never fabricate), designation_id (long, resolve via designation lookup - never fabricate). Always resolve location and designation names to their IDs. Do not fabricate any IDs.' },
  { tool: 'addCase', purpose: 'Use this tool when the user wants to raise, submit, or create a new HR helpdesk case or HR query. Trigger phrases: raise a case, submit a case, create a case, add a case, open a ticket, log a helpdesk request, I have an HR query, raise an HR request.  REQUIRED first step: call getCaseAddSettings. Its response contains two values you MUST read before collecting any user input: - isPriorityRestricted: if true, do NOT ask for priority and do NOT include the priority param. If false, ask the user: Low (10), Medium (11), High (12). - isDescrMandated: if true, description is mandatory - ask for it. If false, description is optional.  These two values from getCaseAddSettings directly control which parameters you collect from the user and pass to this tool. You cannot correctly fill this form without calling getCaseAddSettings first.  Then call listAllCategory to resolve categoryId. Collect subject and other applicable fields. Confirm before submitting.  ATTACHMENTS: if the user attached files in this chat and wants them on the case, for EACH file call useChatFileInField with moduleName=\'HRCase\' and the chat fileId from the [Attached files: ...] context; collect each response\'s fileId, fileName and fileSize and pass them in this tool\'s case_attachment parameter as a JSON array of objects - the returned fileId as filePath, plus fileName and fileSize. Max 5 files. NEVER pass raw chat fileIds into case_attachment.  If the response returns status=Failure with a message about description being required or empty, ask the user to provide a description and resubmit.\n\ndependencyTools: getCaseAddSettings, listAllCategory, listCaseSubCategories, useChatFileInField' },
  { tool: 'addClient', purpose: 'This action is to create a client. clientName is name of client, currency is currency of client, billingMethod is either hourly job rate or hourly user rate or hourly user rate - jobs or hourly user rate - projects' },
  { tool: 'addCompoffRecord', purpose: 'Creates a compensatory off request (POST /api/v3/leave-tracker/compensatory). Resolve employee name to erecno via getEmployeeBasicDetails; never take erecno from raw user text. Do not call getCompoffRecords before create - that list tool is only for edit/cancel id resolution.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'addDepartmentObjective', purpose: 'Adds a new department-level objective in OKR. Requires objective (name, max 300 chars), visibility (0 or 1), fromDate, and toDate. Optional: description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int), departmentId (JSON array of department IDs, max 10). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrDepartments].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrDepartments' },
  { tool: 'addDependent', purpose: 'This action is used to add a new dependent for benefits.' },
  { tool: 'addFeedback', purpose: 'This action is used to add feedback for a given employee. It requires the employee\'s erecno and the feedback details, whether the given feedback is anonymous or not(if anonymous true or false boolean value) and fetch feedback type from `getFeedbackCategories` and map the typeName recieved from the request and send the mapped typeId while sending the request\n\ndependencyTools: getFeedbackCategories' },
  { tool: 'addHoliday', purpose: 'Admin only. Use when the user wants to create or add a new organization holiday (name, dates, location/shift applicability, restricted holiday, etc.).      If the user has not mentioned a holiday date (or asks to add from gallery / pick a holiday), first call listHolidayGallery (method=gallery_list) and show the gallery holidays for the user to choose; then call this tool with holiday_name, from_date, and to_date taken from the selected gallery entry. Do not invent dates. listHolidayGallery is conditional only - not a hard dependencyTool - so skip it when the user already supplied name and dates.      If the user already provides name and dates, call this tool directly (still resolve location IDs via getLocationDetails when locations are named). Do not use for listing holidays (listholidays) or editing an existing one (editHoliday). Never invent IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'addJobSchedule', purpose: 'This action is to add a job schedules for a job for the user on a specific date, date specifies on which date its has to be added default current date in yyyy-MM-dd format. fromtime is start of job and totime is end of the job that is scheduled, jobId is id for the job for which scheduled is added, jobId can be fetched from the getjobs tool by searching with job name if its having multiple jobs option given to user to choose the job, isPublish is true when user want to publish the job or it will be saved as draft, assignedTo is employee for whom the job schedule is added. add a job schedule for 6th job for next days of timer 10 am to 12 pm.     isRepeat specify if the job schedule needs to be repeated, repeatUntil is mandatory if isRepeat is true specify the date until when the job schedule needs to be repeated, repeatType is mandatory if isRepeat is true values are daily or weekly or monthly, repeatInterval specify the interval for which the job schedule needs to be repeated and is Mandatory if isRepeat is true and values are between 1 to 12\n\ndependencyTools: getJobs' },
  { tool: 'addKeyResult', purpose: 'Adds a new key result to an objective. Requires objectiveId (long), keyResult (name, max 300 chars), fromDate, toDate, progressType (Percentage|Metric), frequencyType (Week|Month), frequencyOption (JSON array of ints from getCheckInFrequencyOptions), and keyOwners (JSON array of employee erecnos). Optional: description (max 3000 chars), metricType (Increase|Decrease, required if progressType is Metric), weightage (int), keReFromProg (int), keReToProg (int). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getCheckInFrequencyOptions].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getCheckInFrequencyOptions' },
  { tool: 'addLeaveGrant', purpose: 'Use when the user wants to create or submit a new leave grant / credit leave units to an employee for a leave type. Do not use for applying leave or adding holidays. Resolve employee via getEmployeeBasicDetails and leave type via fetchLeaveTypes; never take IDs from raw user text. If a supporting file is attached, call uploadTimeAttendanceFile first. Do not call getLeaveGrants before create - that list tool is only for edit/cancel id resolution.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchLeaveTypes, getEmployeeBasicDetails, uploadTimeAttendanceFile' },
  { tool: 'addLeaveType', purpose: 'Creates a leave type: POST JSON whose root key is \'leavetype\' containing the full configuration object.          LOW-FRICTION: Only \'name\' must be collected first; if missing, ask once and show a minimal sample payload. Do not ask follow-up questions for other omitted fields. Never refuse with mandatory-field errors except for missing \'name\'-merge SAFE DEFAULTS into a complete payload and POST. Users may override any field when they specify it (validityTo, description, credit rules, booking limits, duration flags, etc.). Never invent department, location, designation, role, or user IDs.          SAFE DEFAULTS (apply each omitted field; user values win):     - code: three uppercase letters from name (adjust last letter if collision risk).     - type PAID; unit DAY; validityFrom: today yyyy-MM-dd.     - applicable: Users {mode:1,list:[\'-1\']}; Departments, Genders, Designations, Locations, Roles, MaritalStatus each {mode:1,list:[]} (all employees).     - effectiveAfterUnit YEAR; effectiveAfterPeriod 0.     - creditCount 12; creditFrequency YEARLY; resetFrequency YEARLY.     - carryForward {enable:false,maxUnit:0}; encashment {enable:false,maxUnit:0}; exceedBalance {allow:false}.     - weekendAsLeave -1; holidayAsLeave -1.     - allowFullDay true; allowHalfDay true; allowQuarterDay false; allowHour false.     - pastBooking {day:0}; futureBooking {day:0,applyBefore:0}; minLeave 0; maxLeave 0; fileUpload 0.          APPLICABLE SHAPE: Seven keys (MaritalStatus, Departments, Genders, Designations, Locations, Roles, Users); each {mode: 1 include | 0 exclude, list: string ids}. list [\'-1\'] = all in that category; [] = none scoped. Resolve labels via getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getRecords. If lookup fails, revert that key to its safe default (empty list for that dimension), preserve other dimensions, note under Defaults applied, and do not block.          AFTER SUCCESS (same turn, mandatory): fetchLeaveTypeDetails(newId). Present in order: (1) success line with name and id; (2) Defaults applied bullets for each auto-filled field (omit section if the user supplied every field); (3) readable summary from fetchLeaveTypeDetails grouped as Basics, Credit/Reset, Booking, Policy, Applicable (Users [\'-1\'] decodes to all users); (4) hint: editLeaveType. If fetchLeaveTypeDetails fails: still (1), (2), and the exact payload sent. Never end with only an id or raw JSON.' },
  { tool: 'addLocationObjective', purpose: 'Adds a new location-level objective in OKR. Requires objective (name, max 300 chars), visibility (0 or 1), fromDate, and toDate. Optional: description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int), locationId (long). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrLocations].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrLocations' },
  { tool: 'addOnDuty', purpose: 'Submit an on-duty request for work outside office (client visits, meetings, events). Do not ask confirmation  -  proceed directly.      Two modes based on unit param:      Mode 1 (unit=0, day-based): dataObj per date has dayTaken (0=full, 1=half, 2=quarter) and session. Full day: no session. Half: session 1 or 2. Quarter: session 1-4. Default: full day.      Mode 2 (unit=1, hours-based): dataObj per date has ftime/ttime in mins from midnight (09:00AM=540, 02:00PM=840).       IMPORTANT  -  On-duty disambiguation (run this BEFORE step 0 whenever the user just says \'apply on-duty\' / \'on-duty request\' without explicitly choosing attendance OD vs an on-duty leave):      a. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods  -  Attendance On-Duty is available iff is_on_duty_enabled == true.      b. Call getLeaveBalance for the same erecno  -  Leave-type On-Duty is available iff any entry in the leavetypes array has typeConstant == \'ON_DUTY\' (equivalently type == 1).      c. Route based on what is available:         - Only Attendance OD available -> continue with this tool (addOnDuty) using the steps below.         - Only Leave-type On-Duty available -> do NOT call this tool; hand off to applyLeave using that ON_DUTY leave type\'s leaveTypeId.         - Both available -> ASK the user which one they want: \'Attendance on-duty request\' or \'On-Duty leave\'. Only after the user picks, proceed with the matching tool.         - Neither available -> tell the user on-duty is not enabled for them and stop.      Skip this disambiguation only when the user\'s wording already pins the path (e.g., \'attendance OD\', \'OD request\', \'client visit OD\' -> this tool; \'apply on-duty leave\', \'on-duty leave for ...\' -> applyLeave).       Before invoking (Attendance OD path):      0. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods. Proceed only if is_on_duty_enabled is true; otherwise tell the user on-duty requests are disabled.      1. Call getAllODTypes. One type = use it. Multiple = fuzzy-match user input; ask only if no match.      2. Pick mode: from/to times -> unit=1, else unit=0 (default full day).      3. type=\'addData\'.      4. startDate/endDate in dd-MMM-yyyy (same for single day).      5. dateFormat=\'dd-MMM-yyyy\'.      6. dataObj: keys=date strings (dd-MMM-yyyy), values=mode-specific fields.      7. Pass desc only if user explicitly provides a reason.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsMethods, getAllODTypes, getLeaveBalance' },
  { tool: 'addOrgCompetencies', purpose: 'Creates new competencies at the organisation level. The competencies parameter is required and must be a JSON array of competency objects following the addorg template in which name param for competency name and description param for competency description alone should be used.' },
  { tool: 'addOrgKras', purpose: 'Creates new KRAs at the organisation level. The kras parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA objects following the addkraorg template in which name param for kra name , description param for kra description , maximum_range param for kra weightage maximum range and minimum_range param for kra weightage minimum range alone should be used. In response show type key represents 0 as Organisation KRA , 2 as User KRA' },
  { tool: 'addOrgObjective', purpose: 'Adds a new organization-level objective in OKR. Requires objective (name, max 300 chars), visibility (0 or 1), fromDate, and toDate. Optional: description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData' },
  { tool: 'addOrgReviewQuestions', purpose: 'Adds new review questions to the organisation. The questions parameter is required and must be a JSON array of question objects following the addquestionorg template in which question param alone must be used ,it should be mandatory.' },
  { tool: 'addOrgSkills', purpose: 'Creates new skills at the organisation level. The skills parameter is required and must be a JSON array of skill objects following the add template in which name param for skill name and description param for skill description alone should be used.' },
  { tool: 'addProvider', purpose: 'This action is used to add a new benefit provider to the organization.' },
  { tool: 'addRecord', purpose: 'This action is used to add a record. It starts by retrieving the formlinkname using the identifyForm tool and then fetches the field details using the getFields tool, based on the formId obtained from identifyForm.      The tool matches the user\'s input with the required fields and constructs the input using the RECORD_ADD_UPDATE PromptSection.      STRICT: For Lookup fields, call getLookupOptions with the relevant labelname values in the fields parameter. The response contains lookupOptions where each field labelname maps to an array of { Value, Id } objects. Match the user\'s text against Value and send the corresponding Id. NEVER send display strings for Lookup fields.      For Picklist and Dropdown fields, call getFieldOptions with the relevant labelname values to fetch available options. Match the user\'s input against the option values (case-sensitive). If an exact match is found, send the matched option value as-is. If no exact match is found, present the available options to the user and ask whether they want to choose from the existing options or quick-add the provided value as a new option.      STRICT: For Gender, BloodGroup and Country fields, call getFieldOptions with the relevant labelname values to fetch available options. The response contains an Options object where keys are internal identifiers and values are the display option texts (e.g., Options: {Option1: Male, Option2: Female, Option3: Others}). Match the user\'s input against the option values (case-sensitive). If an exact match is found, send the matched option value as-is. If no exact match is found, present the available options to the user and ask them to choose. NEVER send a value that is not present in the fetched options list.      If a Lookup Id cannot be resolved, ask the user to choose from available options or provide the ID instead of proceeding with a string value.      STRICT: For file or image fields, NEVER pass a raw chat fileId from `[Attached files: ...]`. First call useChatFileInField to bridge the chat file and obtain a new ZFS fileId; place that returned fileId in inputData for the file/image field AND set isFileId=true on this addRecord call so the value is treated as a raw fileId instead of an encrypted token. If no file/image field is being assigned a fileId in this call, omit isFileId (default false).      The final data is formatted as a string and passed as inputData to complete the record creation process.      POST-SUCCESS URL RULE (STRICT): After this call succeeds, MUST NOT emit ANY URL or \'View Your Record\' / \'Open <form> Record\' link to the just-created record - there is no per-single-record view URL tool. Confirm success in plain language; optionally offer to open the records listing page and only call getRecordsViewUrl if the user confirms (use its returned URL verbatim). See OUTPUT_HYGIENE_GUARD rule 6.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getFields, getFieldOptions, getLookupOptions' },
  { tool: 'addRegularization', purpose: 'Submit a regularization request to correct missed/incorrect attendance entries. All dates: dd-MMM-yyyy format.      Before invoking:      0. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods. Proceed only if is_regularization_enabled is true; otherwise tell the user regularization is disabled.      1. Call getAllRegReasons. If reasons exist, fuzzy-match user\'s choice to exact list entry. If empty, omit reasonanddesc from data.      2. Collect date, check-in/out times, and reason (from the valid list if applicable) from user.      3. Convert times to mins from midnight (09:00 AM=540, 06:00 PM=1080).      4. Set type=\'addData\'.      5. startDate and endDate in dd-MMM-yyyy (same for single day).      6. dateFormat=\'dd-MMM-yyyy\'.      7. regFromTime/regToTime = check-in/out in mins.      8. attendDate = date being regularized (dd-MMM-yyyy).      9. data = JSON keyed by date (dd-MMM-yyyy). Each entry: {ftime, ttime, fromDate, toDate, reasonanddesc:{reason:"..."}}. Omit reasonanddesc if reasons not enforced.      10. IMPORTANT: URL-encode the data parameter value before passing.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsMethods, getAllRegReasons' },
  { tool: 'addShiftChangeRequest', purpose: 'This tool is used to create/submit a shift change request to change the user\'s assigned shift.      Do not ask for confirmation before submitting. Directly proceed with the request using the available information.      Before invoking this tool:      1. Pass erecno of the employee whose shift is being changed. This tool supports multiple users in a single call. If multiple users need the same shift change (same shift, same dates), pass all their erecnos as a comma-separated string in a single call. Do NOT call this tool separately for each user when the shift and dates are identical.      2. Fetch applicable shifts using getApplicableShiftsForUser tool. If only one shift is available, use it directly. If the user specifies a shift name, fuzzy match it against the available shifts and use the closest match. If no match is found, ask the user to select from the available shifts.      3. Pass shiftid with the ID of the target shift from getApplicableShiftsForUser.      4. Pass fdate (start date) and tdate (end date) in dd-MMM-yyyy format. For single day shift change, both should be the same.      5. Pass dateFormat as \'dd-MMM-yyyy\'.      6. Pass desc only if the user explicitly provides a reason. Do not auto-generate or infer a reason.      7. Always pass update=\'true\' and updateAttEntries=\'true\'.\n\ndependencyTools: getApplicableShiftsForUser' },
  { tool: 'addSubKeyResult', purpose: 'Adds a sub key result under a parent key result. Requires objectiveId (long), parentKeyId (long), keyResult (name, max 300 chars), fromDate, toDate, progressType (Percentage|Metric), frequencyType (Week|Month), frequencyOption (JSON array of ints), and keyOwners (JSON array of employee erecnos). Optional: description (max 3000 chars), metricType (Increase|Decrease), weightage (int), keReFromProg (int), keReToProg (int). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getParentKeyResults, getCheckInFrequencyOptions].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getParentKeyResults, getCheckInFrequencyOptions' },
  { tool: 'addTimelog', purpose: 'This action is to add timelog or log time for a user, it is a mandatory field always fetch it from the current user\'s erecno and pass it as an argument in all cases or the mentioned user\'s erecno, jobName is a job that time is logged, user is the Employee for whom time logs is added default is current user, workDate is the date to log time (derive from today\'s date from system instruction\'s DATE section and convert to yyyy-MM-dd format), hours is duration for the timelog, fromTime is start and endTime is end of time log, billingStatus is either billable or non-billable default value is billable and is mandatory field, dateFormat is the format of workDate that is used. jobId is id of job and will be given priority to this in place of jobName if both are available\n\ndependencyTools: getJobs' },
  { tool: 'addUpdateDeptStreamHead', purpose: 'Assigns or updates the stream head for a specific stream within a department. Resolve $departmentId$ via getDepartmentDetails and $streamId$ via getStreamOptions. Pass user_id as the employee record number of the employee to set as the stream head, resolve the user_id via getEmployeeBasicDetails; never take user_id directly from raw user input. Confirm the assignment with the user before invoking.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getStreamOptions, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'addUserBeneficiary', purpose: 'Adds a beneficiary to an employee\'s enrollment.      SELF USAGE: Use the current user\'s erecno when adding beneficiaries to their own enrollment.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: Resolve the target employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'addUserObjective', purpose: 'Adds a new user-level objective in OKR. Requires objective (name, max 300 chars), owner (employee erecno, long), fromDate, and toDate. Optional: description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData' },
  { tool: 'addWFHRequest', purpose: 'Submit a Work From Home (WFH) / Remote Work / WFH Exception request. Do not ask for confirmation  -  proceed directly.      Before invoking:      1. Call getWFHPolicyInfo to check available balance and policy constraints.      2. If availableDays is 0, inform the user they have exhausted their WFH/Remote Work quota and cannot apply.      3. If isWfhReasonsEnabled is true, fuzzy-match the user\'s reason to the closest entry in wfhReasons array. Only ask the user to clarify if no reasonable match can be found.      4. If isDescriptionMandatory is true, ensure the user provides a description.      5. Check restrictedWeekdays  -  if the requested date falls on a restricted weekday, inform the user.      Parameters:      - sDate: start date in dd-MMM-yyyy format      - eDate: end date in dd-MMM-yyyy format (same as sDate for single day)\n\ndependencyTools: getWFHPolicyInfo' },
  { tool: 'alignObjective', purpose: 'Aligns an objective with another objective. Requires objectiveId (long) and alignToObjectiveId (long). Use getObjectiveForAlign first to get available objectives for alignment. Dependencies: [getObjectiveForAlign].\n\ndependencyTools: getObjectiveForAlign' },
  { tool: 'allCaseslist', purpose: 'get all HR cases listing for the user if the index is not mentioned always send index=0' },
  { tool: 'applyLeave', purpose: 'Applies for a leave on behalf of the user.      Before invoking this tool:         1. Call fetchLeaveBasicInfo to fetch the formlinkname for the leave form.         2. Use the formlinkname to call getFields and identify all mandatory fields.         3. Use getLeaveBalance to retrieve the list of applicable leave types and balances.         4. Display only leave type names to the user. Internally, map the user-selected leave type name to its corresponding long leaveTypeId before building the addRecord request.Leave types must be shown only as a clean selectable list (one per line or numbered).         5. Always determine the correct erecno from context:            - Use the current user\'s erecno if no name is mentioned.            - If another person (e.g., \'Ramesh\') is mentioned, resolve their erecno from employee context.            Never take this value directly from user input.         6. Call leavePreview (dependency) with the resolved employee, leave type id, from, to, and dayDetails to confirm balance impact before submit.            Always show the preview\'s current balance, balance after booking, and year end balance to the user before submission.         7. Construct an inputData object using these field label names as keys: Employee_ID, Leavetype, From, To.            Include any other mandatory fields from getFields (for example Reason) when they are present.            The Employee_ID field MUST ALWAYS contain the resolved erecno. The Employee_ID value MUST NEVER be taken from user input under any circumstance.            The Leavetype field MUST ALWAYS contain the resolved leaveTypeId. The Leavetype value MUST NEVER be taken from user input under any circumstance.            From and To must be date strings in the organization\'s date display format (use dateFormat from system instruction\'s DATE section).         8. DAYS: If half-day, quarter-day, full-day, or hour-based leave is mentioned, add \'days\' in inputData (date keys in org date format). The JSON below is a format example only - never reuse these dates or values; always build days from the user\'s requested dates, count, and session/time.            Day-based e.g. \'days\':{\'07-Jan-2020\':{\'LeaveCount\':0.5, \'Session\':2}}            LeaveCount: 1 full day (omit Session); 0.5 half day (Session 1=first half, 2=second half); 0.25 quarter day (Session 1, 2, 3, or 4).            Hour-based e.g. \'days\':{\'07-Jan-2021\':{\'LeaveCount\':\'01:00\', \'StartTime\':\'17:00\', \'EndTime\':\'18:00\'}}          9. Finally, format this object into a string and pass it as inputData.            And the dependent tools should not be re-invoked unnecessarily if the formlinkname and balance data are already available.            On successful applyLeave, get the id from the apply response (the record id for the leave that was just applied) and use it to show the applied leave details to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchLeaveBasicInfo, getFields, getLeaveBalance, getLeaveRecords, leavePreview' },
  { tool: 'applyPermission', purpose: 'This tool is used to create/submit a permission request to cover non-worked time within the maximum allowed permission duration defined by the organization.      Do not ask for confirmation before submitting. Directly proceed with the request using the available information.      Before invoking this tool:      0. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods. Proceed only if is_permission_enabled is true; otherwise tell the user permission requests are disabled.      1. Fetch applicable permission types using getApplicablePermForUser tool. If only one permission type is available, use it directly. If multiple permission types are available: first try to fuzzy-match the user\'s request context against the available type names (handle typos, partial matches, synonyms, abbreviations). If a match is found, use it. If no reasonable match can be determined, present the available permission types to the user and ask them to select one. Do NOT default to the first type when multiple types exist.      2. Use the date, from-time and to-time provided by the user in their request.      3. Convert from-time and to-time to minutes from midnight (e.g., 02:00 PM = 840, 03:00 PM = 900, 11:30 AM = 690).      4. Construct the input JSON object with all values as strings: erecno, date (dd-MMM-yyyy), permissionId (from getApplicablePermForUser), fromTime (mins from midnight), toTime (mins from midnight), and reason (if provided).\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsMethods, getApplicablePermForUser' },
  { tool: 'approvalReject', purpose: 'This action is used to approve or reject a record.pkid is a UUID number that is used to identify the approval,     status is regex used to approve or reject an request,remarks are the comments that are given by the user while approving/rejecting.\n\ndependencyTools: getApprovals' },
  { tool: 'approveEnrollment', purpose: 'This action is used to approve a pending enrollment request.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollments' },
  { tool: 'archiveUserGoals', purpose: 'Archives or unarchives goals for a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment; if the employee is not specified, use the logged-in user\'s erecno. goal_ids is a required JSON array of goal IDs obtained from getUserGoals - call getUserGoals with status=0 to list active goals when archiving, or status=8 to list archived goals when unarchiving. archive=true archives the goals; archive=false unarchives them. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserGoals]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserGoals' },
  { tool: 'bookedAndBalance', purpose: 'Use this when the user asks for leave balance, booked vs balance, or which leave type has more/less balance for a period.      Standalone tool - not a dependency of applyLeave. Do not use for apply-leave preview; that is leavePreview.' },
  { tool: 'cancelLeave', purpose: 'Use when the user wants to cancel or withdraw an already submitted leave request. Do not use for cancel leave grant (cancelLeaveGrant) or cancel comp-off (cancelcompoff). Resolve record_id from getLeaveRecords; collect cancellation reason when needed.\n\ndependencyTools: getLeaveRecords' },
  { tool: 'cancelLeaveGrant', purpose: 'Use when the user wants to cancel or withdraw an existing leave grant request. Do not use to cancel leave (use cancelLeave) or to edit a grant (use editLeaveGrant). Resolve record_id from getLeaveGrants; never invent or accept unchecked numeric IDs from the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getLeaveGrants' },
  { tool: 'cancelRegularization', purpose: 'Cancels one or more previously submitted regularization requests. The caller can cancel only their own requests (unless they are admin / SPOC / approver for that record). Use when the user says they want to cancel/withdraw a regularization they submitted. ALWAYS confirm with the user (show the date/time/reason of the record being cancelled) before calling  -  cancellation is immediate and cannot be undone from the API.      Before invoking:      1. Call getApprovals with action=\'myRequests\' (or action=\'myApprovals\' if the user is approving). Match the user\'s description (date, reason, status) against the returned records and resolve recordId.      2. recordId accepts a single numeric id, or multiple ids as a comma-separated string for batch cancellation.      3. Pass reason only if the user explicitly supplies one; otherwise omit it.      If the record is already in CANCELLED status the API returns an ALREADYCANCEL response; if DELETED, INVALIDRECORD; if the user does not own the record and is not admin/approver/SPOC, PERMDENIED. Surface these messages to the user without retrying.\n\ndependencyTools: getApprovals' },
  { tool: 'cancelcompoff', purpose: 'Cancels an existing compensatory off request. Resolve record_id from getCompoffRecords before invoking; never invent IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: getCompoffRecords' },
  { tool: 'changeCaseCategory', purpose: 'Use this tool when the user wants to change or update the category OR subcategory of an HR helpdesk case. Trigger phrases: \'change case category\', \'update category\', \'move case to another category\', \'change subcategory\', \'update subcategory\', \'reassign category\'. FOUR scenarios: (A) Both zp_recordId AND categoryId are known - call this tool directly. (B) zp_recordId is NOT provided - use dependency tools to show the user\'s cases, ask them to pick one, then proceed. (C) categoryId is NOT provided - use dependency tools to fetch all categories, display them, ask the user to pick one. (D) User wants to change ONLY the subcategory - use dependency tools to get the current categoryId, then list available subcategories, ask the user to pick one, then call this tool. Optional: subCategoryId=0 if no subcategory.\n\ndependencyTools: listAllCategory, listMyCases, listMyRequests, viewCase, listCaseSubCategories' },
  { tool: 'changeCasePriority', purpose: 'Use this tool when the user wants to change or update the priority of an HR helpdesk case. Trigger phrases: \'change case priority\', \'update case priority\', \'set priority\', \'mark case as high priority\', \'set case priority\'. Priority values: 10=Low, 11=Medium, 12=High. TWO scenarios: (A) If the user already provided a zp_recordId - call this tool directly with that zp_recordId and the requested priority. (B) If no record ID is provided - use dependency tools to show the user\'s cases, ask them to pick one, then call this tool with the chosen zp_recordId and priority.\n\ndependencyTools: listMyCases, listMyRequests' },
  { tool: 'changeCaseStatus', purpose: 'Use this tool when the user wants to change or update the status of an HR helpdesk case. Trigger phrases: \'change case status\', \'update case status\', \'mark case as\', \'close case\', \'reopen case\', \'set status\', \'mark as in progress\', \'mark as closed\', \'mark as pending\'. Status values: 1=Open, 2=In Progress, 3=Pending, 4=On Hold, 5=Closed, 6=Cancelled. TWO scenarios: (A) If the user already provided a zp_recordId - call this tool directly with that zp_recordId and the requested status. (B) If no record ID is provided - use dependency tools to show the user\'s cases, ask them to pick one, then call this tool with the chosen zp_recordId and status.\n\ndependencyTools: listMyCases, listMyRequests' },
  { tool: 'changeTaskOwner', purpose: 'This action changes the owner of a task. It requires the taskId and the employee record number (erecno) of the new taskowner.\n\ndependencyTools: getMyTasks, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'checkIn', purpose: 'This tool can be used by by self user alone. No user can use this tool on behalf of another user. This action is used to mark user\'s checkIn/punchIn/End a break.      To mark checkIn/punchIn or end a break:     It starts by retrieving the current attendance status of user using the getStatus tool, retrieve allowedToCheckIn from the response.      If it\'s true only then checkIn action can be allowed else return error  user is already in checked in state.\n\ndependencyTools: getStatus_or_getBreaks' },
  { tool: 'checkOut', purpose: 'This tool can be used by by self user alone. No user can use this tool on behalf of another user. This action is used to mark user\'s checkOut/punchOut/Start a break.      To mark checkOut/punchOut:     It starts by retrieving the current attendance status of user using the getStatus tool, retrieve allowedToCheckIn from the response.      If it\'s false only then checkOut action can be allowed else return error  user is already in checked out state.          To start the break:      First invoke getStatus_or_getBreaks tool and get breakId from user. Use the breakId in checkOut tool parameter to start break\n\ndependencyTools: getStatus_or_getBreaks' },
  { tool: 'checkinKeyResult', purpose: 'Checks in progress for a key result. Requires keyResultId (long), updatedProgress (int), and planId (long, from getCheckInPlanDates). Optional: comment (text, max 3000 chars). Dependencies: [getCheckInPlanDates].\n\ndependencyTools: getCheckInPlanDates' },
  { tool: 'completeEnrollmentWindow', purpose: 'This action is used to complete the enrollment requests for an enrollment window.\n\ndependencyTools: getEnrollmentWindows' },
  { tool: 'completeOnboarding', purpose: 'Marks onboarding as completed by admin for a candidate or employee. HARD CONSTRAINT: for candidates, MUST ONLY work when current status is In Progress or Reopened. For employees, MUST ONLY work when current status is In Progress. If the record\'s current status is not one of these valid states, MUST NOT proceed and MUST tell the user that complete onboarding is not supported for that status - use text labels when informing the user, not status numbers. Call listOnboardingRecords first to find and confirm the record\'s PKID and verify status before invoking (In Progress = ONBOARDING_STATUS 2, Reopened = ONBOARDING_STATUS 5 in the response). Pass the PKID as recordId (longId) and pass \'candidate\' or \'employee\' as obType in the request body. Requires confirmation before executing.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'completeTask', purpose: 'This action changes the status of the task to \'completed\', it requires taskid.\n\ndependencyTools: getMyTasks' },
  { tool: 'createAbsentScheduler', purpose: 'Creates an Absent Scheduler rule (Settings > Automation > Absent Scheduler). Required: name, time, applicable_for (JSON; resolve IDs via getApplicableInfo; for user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo)), push_absent_to_leave (0|1), notify_through_mail (0|1). TIME is packed: offset_days = integer division of time by 1440 (0-5); run_clock_minutes = time minus (offset_days times 1440). Attendance date processed = run_date minus offset_days. Example: 4500 = 3:00 AM run, offset 3, processes attendance 3 days before run date. Encode: time = clock_minutes plus (offset_days times 1440). When notify_through_mail=1, notifications is required and must be non-empty; each entry needs day (1-10) and at least one of notifyEmployee, notifyManager, or specificUsers. Optional: leave_types (fetchLeaveTypes) when push_absent_to_leave=1. notifications[].day (1-10) = consecutive absence streak for email only.\n\ndependencyTools: getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'createBenefitCategory', purpose: 'This action is used to create a new benefit category in the organization.' },
  { tool: 'createBenefitPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to create a new benefit plan in the organization.' },
  { tool: 'createBreak', purpose: 'Creates a break definition. Duration: fixed break_time_in_mins OR accrual break_on_work_hrs (one mode per break, at least one required). ACCRUAL FORMAT: break_on_work_hrs is a JSONArray; each tier object must have ONLY breakTime and workingHrs (both integers in minutes). Example: [{breakTime:15,workingHrs:240},{breakTime:30,workingHrs:360}]. Do NOT use breakMinutes, working_hours, or hours. Both values must strictly increase per tier (max 6 tiers). WINDOW FORMAT: break_res_from_to_time uses ONLY fromTime and toTime (minutes from midnight). Required: break_name, is_break_auto_deduct, applicable_shifts from getShiftInfo. Optional: break_color_code (1-16, default 6), break_image_code (1-8, default 1), break_pay_type (0=unpaid, 1=paid).\n\ndependencyTools: getShiftInfo' },
  { tool: 'createDivision', purpose: 'Creates a new division in the organization structure. Requires \'name\' (mandatory, must be unique within divisions). Optional parameters: \'description\' (text description), \'zp_code\' (unique short code, max 10 characters, no angle brackets), and \'parent_division\' (ID of the parent division for creating nested divisions). Returns the newly created division\'s zoho_id on success. Error codes: 0 = duplicate name, 1 = empty name, 5 = duplicate zp_code, 6 = empty zp_code, 7 = invalid zp_code, 8 = zp_code too long.' },
  { tool: 'createEnrollmentWindow', purpose: 'This action is used to create a new enrollment window.' },
  { tool: 'createEntity', purpose: 'Creates a new legal entity in the organization structure. Requires \'name\' (mandatory, must be unique within legal entities). Optional parameters: \'description\' (text description) and \'zp_code\' (unique short code, max 10 characters, no angle brackets). Returns the newly created entity\'s zoho_id on success. Error codes: 0 = duplicate name, 1 = empty name, 5 = duplicate zp_code, 6 = empty zp_code, 7 = invalid zp_code, 8 = zp_code too long.' },
  { tool: 'createKioskDevice', purpose: 'Creates a Kiosk device login (client-portal user) and sends an account-confirmation email. Requires an existing kiosk portal (call getKioskConfig / upsertKioskPortal first). Required: device_name, email, password. Optional: timezone, country_code, language_code (default to the admin\'s), is_dynamic_punch_enabled (auto show check-in or check-out by current status), is_delete_captured_image_enabled.\n\ndependencyTools: getKioskConfig' },
  { tool: 'createPermissionRule', purpose: 'Creates a new hour-permission rule. For viewing an existing rule\'s details use listPermissionRules then getPermissionRule  -  not this action.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=permission)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Collect required fields from the user: permission_name, period_type (valid values: 1=weekly, 2=monthly), allowed_time_in_mins, is_applicable_to_all. When not applicable to all, also collect applicable_fields (include/exclude arrays resolved via dependency tools  -  never ask the user for raw IDs).         After calling:         3. Call getPermissionRule with the returned permission_id once to confirm the rule was created; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, listPermissionRules, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'createPlanYear', purpose: 'This action is used to create a new plan year.' },
  { tool: 'createPresentByDefault', purpose: 'Creates a Present by Default group. Applicable employees are auto-marked Present daily without manual check-in/out (absent scheduler exempt; leave overrides). Required: name, from_date (org date format), reason (non-empty text stored on the group). Optional: to_date (omit for open-ended), is_applicable_to_all (true = all employees), applicable_for (JSON with user/loc/dept/desg/role/entity/business_unit/division/level ID arrays; resolve IDs via getApplicableInfo; use user:["0"] for all employees).\n\ndependencyTools: getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'createRemotePolicy', purpose: 'Creates a new remote work policy.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=remotepolicy)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Collect required fields from the user: policy name, applicable_to ({ type, ids }  -  type is one of employee/location/department/designation/role, resolve IDs via dependency tools  -  never ask the user for raw IDs), and the policy rule fields: type (1=employee raises request, 2=auto-approved), limit_restricted (cap remote days per period; if true, also collect days and period where 1=weekly 2=monthly), remote_approval_type (1=mandatory, 2=allow without approval for allowed days, 3=allow without approval + require request for excess), reason_mandatory, is_wfh_reason_enabled (if true, also collect wfh_reasons as comma-separated values). When is_wfh_reason_enabled is true, wfh_reasons must include at least one non-empty reason.         After calling:         3. Call getRemotePolicy with the returned policy_id once to confirm the policy was created; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'createSpecificPolicy', purpose: 'Creates a new specific attendance policy.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams with mode=specificpolicy  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values.         2. Determine applicability by fuzzy matching user input to IDs using dependency tools  -  use getApplicableInfo for user, employee_type, department, and designation; use getShiftInfo for shift. Payload must include applicable_to: {type, ids} where type is one of user, employee_type, department, designation, or shift.         Round-off vs Grace period (two completely separate features):         3. Round-off fields (early_check_in_round_off, late_check_in_round_off, early_check_out_round_off, late_check_out_round_off, and their *_mins variants)  -  adjusts the recorded punch time toward the shift boundary; it does NOT deduct leave. *_round_off=true snaps fully to the boundary; *_mins=N snaps only if within N minutes.         4. Grace period field (grace_period)  -  deducts leave when attendance violations exceed a configured frequency; it does NOT change the recorded punch time. grace_period is {rules:[{Intime, Outtime, Worktime, Coretime, allowDays, graceMode, period, redStat, leavetype}]}. Dimensions are determined by which time fields are present: Intime (late check-in), Outtime (early check-out), Worktime (work-hours deficit), Coretime (core-hours violation). Only add Worktime or Coretime if explicitly requested. period is int enum ONLY: 0=weekly, 1=monthly, 2=pay-period  -  NEVER a count of days; when user says "7 days" map to allowDays:7, not period:7. Never mix round-off with grace period  -  a late check-in tolerance goes inside a rule\'s Intime, not in late_check_in_mins.         After calling:         5. Call getSpecificPolicyDetail with the returned settings_id once to confirm the policy was created; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getShiftInfo, getApplicableInfo, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'createUnit', purpose: 'Creates a new business unit in the organization structure. Requires \'name\' (mandatory, must be unique within business units). Optional parameters: \'description\' (text description) and \'zp_code\' (unique short code, max 10 characters, no angle brackets). Returns the newly created unit\'s zoho_id on success. Error codes: 0 = duplicate name, 1 = empty name, 5 = duplicate zp_code, 6 = empty zp_code, 7 = invalid zp_code, 8 = zp_code too long.' },
  { tool: 'deleteAbsentScheduler', purpose: 'Permanently deletes an absent scheduler by record_id (path). Resolve record_id via listAbsentSchedulers. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.\n\ndependencyTools: listAbsentSchedulers' },
  { tool: 'deleteBreak', purpose: 'Permanently deletes a break definition by record_id (path). Resolve record_id via listBreaks. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.\n\ndependencyTools: listBreaks' },
  { tool: 'deleteCandidate', purpose: 'Permanently deletes a candidate from the onboarding module. HARD CONSTRAINT: this action permanently removes the candidate record and cannot be undone - MUST ask for explicit confirmation before proceeding. Call listOnboardingRecords first to find the candidate and obtain their PKID. Pass the PKID as deletegroup (long) in the request body. Do NOT use CID - it is an internal sequence number and will fail. MUST tell the user the candidate name and ask them to confirm deletion before invoking. Never fabricate the candidate ID.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'deleteDeptStreamHead', purpose: 'Removes the stream head assigned to a specific stream within a department. Resolve $departmentId$ via getDepartmentDetails and $streamId$ via getStreamOptions before invoking. Confirm the removal with the user before invoking.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getStreamOptions' },
  { tool: 'deleteKeyResult', purpose: 'Deletes a specific key result. Requires keyResultId (long). Ask for consent before performing this action.' },
  { tool: 'deleteKioskDevice', purpose: 'Permanently deletes a kiosk login device by device id (path). Resolve the device id via getKioskLoginUsers. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.\n\ndependencyTools: getKioskLoginUsers' },
  { tool: 'deleteKraGoals', purpose: 'Deletes goal mappings from a given KRA for a specific employee. The goal and kra parameters are required. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras, getKraGoals]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras, getKraGoals' },
  { tool: 'deleteObjective', purpose: 'Deletes an existing objective. Requires objectiveId (long). Ask for consent before performing this action. Dependencies: [getObjectiveDetails].\n\ndependencyTools: getObjectiveDetails' },
  { tool: 'deleteOrgCompetencies', purpose: 'Deletes competencies from the organisation. The competency_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of competency IDs to delete. Dependencies: [getOrgCompetencies]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgCompetencies' },
  { tool: 'deleteOrgKras', purpose: 'Deletes KRAs from the organisation. The type parameter specifies whether to delete an org KRA (kra) or user KRA (userKra). The kra_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA IDs to delete. Dependencies: [getOrgKras]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgKras' },
  { tool: 'deleteOrgReviewQuestions', purpose: 'Deletes review questions from the organisation. The question_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of question IDs to delete. Dependencies: [getOrgReviewQuestions]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgReviewQuestions' },
  { tool: 'deleteOrgSkills', purpose: 'Deletes skills from the organisation. The skill_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of skill IDs to delete. Dependencies: [getOrgSkills]. Kindly ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgSkills' },
  { tool: 'deletePermissionRule', purpose: 'Deletes an hour-permission rule permanently. Once deleted the rule no longer applies to any employee.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call listPermissionRules to resolve the rule by name  -  never ask the user for a numeric permission_id.         After calling:         2. Attempt getPermissionRule with the deleted id once. If not found, confirm deletion to the user; otherwise report the discrepancy explicitly.\n\ndependencyTools: listPermissionRules, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'deletePresentByDefault', purpose: 'Permanently deletes a present-by-default group. Resolve record_id via listPresentByDefault. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.\n\ndependencyTools: listPresentByDefault' },
  { tool: 'deleteRemotePolicy', purpose: 'Deletes a remote work policy permanently. Deletion removes the policy and all its applicability mappings.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getRemotePolicies to resolve the policy by name  -  never ask the user for a numeric policy_id.         After calling:         2. Attempt getRemotePolicy with the deleted id once. If not found, confirm deletion to the user; otherwise report the discrepancy explicitly.\n\ndependencyTools: getRemotePolicies, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'deleteSpecificPolicy', purpose: 'Hard-deletes a specific attendance policy identified by settings_id (path segment), including its applicability mappings. Resolve settings_id via getSpecificPolicies from the policy name. Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getSpecificPolicies, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'deleteTimelogs', purpose: 'This action is to delete timelogs, timeLogId is Mandatory field,  It starts by retrieving the time log using getTimelogs tool for a certain period and send the timelog ids as comma seperated values\n\ndependencyTools: getTimelogs' },
  { tool: 'deleteUserCompetencies', purpose: 'Deletes competencies tagged to a specific employee. The user_competency_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of user competency IDs to delete. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Use zoho_id from the response of getUserCompetencies. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserCompetencies]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserCompetencies' },
  { tool: 'deleteUserGoals', purpose: 'Deletes goals for a specific employee. The goal_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of goal IDs to delete. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserGoals]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserGoals' },
  { tool: 'deleteUserKras', purpose: 'Deletes KRAs tagged to a specific employee. The user_kra_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of user KRA IDs to delete. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Use zoho_id from the response of getUserKras. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras' },
  { tool: 'deleteUserSkills', purpose: 'Deletes skills tagged to a specific employee. The user_skill_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of user skill IDs to delete. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Use zoho_id from the response of getUserSkills. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills]. Ask for consent before performing this action\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills' },
  { tool: 'denyEnrollment', purpose: 'This action is used to deny a pending enrollment request.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollments' },
  { tool: 'disableBenefitPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to disable a benefit plan.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'disableEnrollmentWindow', purpose: 'This action is used to disable an enrollment window.\n\ndependencyTools: getEnrollmentWindows' },
  { tool: 'disablePlanYear', purpose: 'This action is used to disable a plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'editCompoffRecord', purpose: 'Updates an existing compensatory off request. Resolve record_id via getCompoffRecords; never invent IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: getCompoffRecords, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'editHoliday', purpose: 'Admin only. Use when the user wants to change an existing holiday (name, dates, applicability, restricted flag, reminders, etc.). Do not use for adding a new holiday (addHoliday) or only viewing holidays (listholidays). Resolve holiday_id via listholidays by matching holiday name/date; never invent IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: listholidays, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'editJobSchedule', purpose: 'This action is to edit a existing job schedule,jobScheduleId is id fetched from getJobSchedule tool or addJobSchedule tool, date specifies on which date its has to be changed default current date in yyyy-MM-dd format. fromtime is start of job and totime is end of the job that is scheduled, jobId is id for the job for which scheduled is added takes previous value or value from getJobs tool, isPublish is true when user want to publish the job or it will be saved as draft, assignedTo is employee for whom the job schedule is edited.     isRepeat specify if the job schedule needs to be repeated, repeatUntil is mandatory if isRepeat is true specify the date until when the job schedule needs to be repeated, repeatType is mandatory if isRepeat is true values are daily or weekly or monthly, repeatInterval specify the interval for which the job schedule needs to be repeated and is Mandatory if isRepeat is true and values are between 1 to 12\n\ndependencyTools: getJobSchedule, addJobSchedule, getJobs' },
  { tool: 'editKeyResult', purpose: 'Edits an existing key result. Requires keyResultId (long), keyResult (name, max 300 chars), fromDate, toDate, and keyOwners (JSON array of employee erecnos). Optional: parentKeyId (long), objectiveId (long), description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int), frequencyType (Week|Month), frequencyOption (JSON array of ints). Dependencies: [getKeyResultDetails].\n\ndependencyTools: getKeyResultDetails' },
  { tool: 'editLeaveGrant', purpose: 'Use when the user wants to change or update an existing leave grant (count, effective date, leave type, reason, or supporting document). Do not use to cancel a grant (use cancelLeaveGrant). Resolve record_id via getLeaveGrants; never invent IDs. Upload a new file via uploadTimeAttendanceFile when attaching a document.\n\ndependencyTools: getLeaveGrants, fetchLeaveTypes, getEmployeeBasicDetails, uploadTimeAttendanceFile' },
  { tool: 'editLeaveType', purpose: 'Updates an existing leave type: POST body key \'leavetype\' using the same field model as addLeaveType (mandatory name, code, type PAID|UNPAID, unit DAY|HOUR, validityFrom, applicable; optional fields follow addLeaveType/API).          WORKFLOW:     1. fetchLeaveTypes -> resolve leave type id by matching name (never trust an unchecked user-supplied id).     2. fetchLeaveTypeDetails(id) -> load current server configuration.     3. Merge requested changes onto that full object-preserve every untouched field; if unsure whether omitted keys persist server-side, send the merged complete leavetype JSON, not a sparse partial.     4. Resolve department/location/designation/role/user references via getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getRecords-never fabricate ids.          dependencyTool enforces fetchLeaveTypes + fetchLeaveTypeDetails before editing. Success returns the updated leave type id.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchLeaveTypes, fetchLeaveTypeDetails' },
  { tool: 'editObjective', purpose: 'Edits an existing objective. Requires objectiveId (long), objective (name, max 300 chars), fromDate, and toDate. Optional: description (max 3000 chars), weightage (int), owner (long), approvalStatus (-1|0|1|2), visibility (0|1). Dependencies: [getObjectiveDetails].\n\ndependencyTools: getObjectiveDetails' },
  { tool: 'editOrgCompetencies', purpose: 'Updates existing competencies at the organisation level. The competencies parameter is required and must be a JSON array of competency objects following the editorg template in which zoho_id param for competency id , name param for competency name and description param for competency description alone should be used. Dependencies: [getOrgCompetencies]\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgCompetencies' },
  { tool: 'editOrgKras', purpose: 'Updates existing KRAs at the organisation level. The kras parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA objects following the editkraorg template in which zoho_id param for kra id , name param for kra name , description param for kra description,                      maximum_range param for kra weightage maximum range and minimum_range param for kra weightage minimum range alone should be used. Dependencies: [getOrgKras]\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgKras' },
  { tool: 'editOrgReviewQuestions', purpose: 'Edits existing review questions in the organisation. The questions parameter is required and must be a JSON array of question objects following the editquestionorg template in which zoho_id param for question_id and question param for question. Dependencies: [getOrgReviewQuestions]\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgReviewQuestions' },
  { tool: 'editOrgSkills', purpose: 'Updates existing skills at the organisation level. The skills parameter is required and must be a JSON array of skill objects following the edit template in which zoho_id param for skill id, name param for skill name and description param for skill description alone should be used. Dependencies: [getOrgSkills]\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgSkills' },
  { tool: 'editTimelog', purpose: 'This action is to edit timelog, timeLogId is Mandatory field,  It starts by retrieving the time log using the addTimelog tool or getTimelogs tool, user it is a mandatory field always fetch it from the current user\'s erecno and pass it as an argument in all cases or the mentioned user\'s erecno,jobName is a job that time is logged, user is the Employee for whom time logs is added, workDate is the date to log time (derive from today\'s date from system instruction\'s DATE section and convert to yyyy-MM-dd format), hours is duration for the timelog, fromTime is start and endTime is end of time log, billingStatus is either billable or non-billable default value is billable\n\ndependencyTools: getTimelogs, addTimelog' },
  { tool: 'editUserCompetencies', purpose: 'Edits competencies tagged to a specific employee. The competencies parameter is required and must be a JSON array of competency objects following the edituser template in which zoho_id param for competency user record id , weightage param for weightage alone should be allowed.. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserCompetencies]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserCompetencies' },
  { tool: 'editUserKras', purpose: 'Edits KRAs tagged to a specific employee. The kras parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA objects following the edit template in which zoho_id param for kra user record id , weightage param for weightage alone should be allowed. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras' },
  { tool: 'editUserSkills', purpose: 'Edits skills tagged to a specific employee. The skills parameter is required and must be a JSON array of skill objects following the edituser template in which zoho_id param for skill user record id, level param for skill level alone should be allowed. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills' },
  { tool: 'employeeInsights', purpose: 'Fetch the latest workforce analytics bundle. Return only the fields that correspond to the users request. Do not derive or recompute. If a section is disabled by disableObj or missing, state no data for that section.  For employees currently working by department, use deptReport. This represents the number of employees currently working in each department and is not an attrition report. Do not use deptReport values for people left.  For employees currently working by location, use locReport. This represents the number of employees currently working in each location and is not an attrition report.  For employees currently working by designation, use desigReport. This represents the number of employees currently working in each designation and is not an attrition report.  For gender diversity, use genderReport. This is not an attrition report.  For experience distribution, use expReport. This is not an attrition report.  For age distribution, use ageReport. This is not an attrition report.  For hiring or new joiners, use newJoiningCount. These addition metrics cover the last 6 months based on the payload labels.  For growth summary, use growthObj.  Never mix sections or compute new metrics. Output must mirror the payload fields exactly. If a requested section is empty, reply with no data and include the empty or zero values exactly as present.' },
  { tool: 'enableBenefitPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to enable a benefit plan.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'enableEnrollmentWindow', purpose: 'This action is used to enable an enrollment window.\n\ndependencyTools: getEnrollmentWindows' },
  { tool: 'enablePlanYear', purpose: 'This action is used to enable a plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'fetchApplicableLeaveTypes', purpose: 'Use this tool whenever leave type applicability is required for an employee (self or another person): which leave types apply to them, including grant-based / fixed / experience-based / attendance-based leave types. Pass creditType=GRANT|FIXED|EXPERIENCED|ATTENDANCE when the user asks for a specific policy type (e.g. \'grant based leave types applicable for me\' -> creditType=GRANT). Returns only leave types attached to that employee via active policy. Do not use admin fetchLeaveTypes (settings list) for applicability. Do not use bookedAndBalance just to list applicable types - use this tool first, then pass the returned leave type ids into bookedAndBalance when balance/booked numbers are also needed.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'fetchEmployeeRecordById', purpose: 'Retrieve the employee record for the given record ID.' },
  { tool: 'fetchEmployeeSalaries', purpose: 'This action is used to list of employee\'s compensation details which includes salary, package details, effective from, currencies.Parse zpu[erecno:{id}]zpu associated with this request as erecno and pass it request url.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'fetchForms', purpose: 'Retrieve the list of forms and their details from Zoho People.' },
  { tool: 'fetchLeaveBasicInfo', purpose: 'For any leave related query. This tool is for internal use only and should not be exposed to the user.And use this response as formlinkname for `applyLeave` tool' },
  { tool: 'fetchLeaveTypeDetails', purpose: 'Returns the full configuration for one leave type (basics, validity, credit/reset, applicability, booking limits, weekend/holiday rules, file upload, etc.). Use when the user asks for rules or setup for a named type. Resolve the leave type name to id via fetchLeaveTypes before calling; never invent or parse an id from raw user text.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'fetchLeaveTypes', purpose: 'Lists configured leave types (id, name, color, unit DAY/HOUR, paid/unpaid). Pagination: startIndex (1-based, default 1), limit (default 30). Call first to list types, resolve a name to id, or pick an id before edit/add checks.' },
  { tool: 'fetchRevisions', purpose: 'This action is used to get employees salary revision details which includes Revised Salary, Revised Amount, Revised Percentage, Reason for Revisions, Salary packages' },
  { tool: 'fetchSalaryComponents', purpose: 'This action is used to get configured salary or benefit components list eg, basic pay , HRA, bonus etc. which includes components code, component name, payment frequencies, earning or deduction, calculation type, calculation value.' },
  { tool: 'fetchSalaryPackageComponents', purpose: 'This action is used to find the packageId from the `fetchSalaryPackages` response and get the salary components details configured with it\n\ndependencyTools: fetchSalaryPackages' },
  { tool: 'fetchSalaryPackages', purpose: 'This action is used to get configured salary package details , which includes package name, package applicablities' },
  { tool: 'fetchSingleEmployeeBreakupDetails', purpose: 'This action is used to get specific employee\'s compensation breakup details which includes ctcComponent i.e part of user salary and benefits which is given as additional perk to user eg. bonus, gift card etc.Parse zpu[erecno:{id}]zpu associated with this request as erecno and pass it request url.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'fetchSingleEmployeeRevisions', purpose: 'This action is used to get specific employee salary revision details which includes Revised Salary, Revised Amount, Revised Percentage, Reason for Revisions, Salary packages.Parse zpu[erecno:{id}]zpu associated with this request as erecno and pass it request url.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'fetchSingleEmployeeSalary', purpose: 'This action is used to get specific employee\'s compensation details which includes salary, package details, effective from, currencies.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'fetchTaskComments', purpose: 'This action retrieves the comments for a specific task, along with details of the employees who commented. It requires a taskid.\n\ndependencyTools: getMyTasks' },
  { tool: 'fetchallgroups', purpose: 'This action retrieves all the groups' },
  { tool: 'fetchgroupmembers', purpose: 'Retrieve all the group members from the group. Requires a groupId obtained from the dependency tools.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchallgroups, fetchmygroups' },
  { tool: 'fetchmygroups', purpose: 'This action retrieves the groups associated with the current user' },
  { tool: 'fileModulePermInitialData', purpose: 'For any files related operations. This tool is for internal use only and should not be exposed to the user.And use this response for checking the user permission for `getAllFiles` tool' },
  { tool: 'getAbsentScheduler', purpose: 'Fetches full detail of a single absent scheduler by record_id (path). Response includes name, time, applicable_for, push_absent_to_leave, notify_through_mail, leave_types, and notifications. TIME decode: offset_days = integer division of time by 1440 (0-5); run_clock_minutes = time minus (offset_days times 1440). Attendance date processed = run_date minus offset_days. Example: 4500 = 3:00 AM run, offset 3, processes attendance 3 days before run date. Encode: time = clock_minutes plus (offset_days times 1440). notifications[].day (1-10) = consecutive absence streak for email only. Resolve record_id via listAbsentSchedulers. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo). For leave_types, resolve each leave-type id to its leave-type name via fetchLeaveTypes and never show the raw leave-type id.\n\ndependencyTools: listAbsentSchedulers, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'getAdditionalOptionsSettings', purpose: 'Returns attendance Additional Options (Settings > Additional Options): show_scale_view controls the day-timeline scale view at the bottom of the attendance list view for real-time punch visualization; is_password_protection_enabled requires attendance export files emailed to the admin to be password-encrypted.      DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show raw param names or JSON structures to the user - present values using plain language labels.' },
  { tool: 'getAllFiles', purpose: 'This action retrieves organisation files for listing using default values: fileType=1, start=0, limit=100, fileSortByType=3, isFileSortDesc=true. fileType (1) defines file type, start sets fetch index, and limit caps results. roleId, catId, locationId (comma-separated, limits apply) filter by role, category, or location; employeeId, entityId, unitId, divisionId, deptId filter by org structure. isExpiredFilesView includes expired files if true. filterView is used to filter files based on location, department, entity, unit, and division (location|entity|unit|division|department, default location) When the user query mentions company, always apply the entity filter. searchFileName (no special chars, max 250) and searchFileExtn filter by name/extension. fromDate/toDate set date range. fileSortByType (1-name, 2-created, 3-modified) and isFileSortDesc (true=desc) control sorting. longitude/latitude allow location-based filtering. isFromPolicy filters policy files, orgUserType filters by user type.          Before invoking this tool:          1) Strictly call fileModulePermInitialData to retrieve the user\'s permissions for the Files module.          2) From the response, read the loginUserRoleCheck parameter:           2.1) If the value is -1, pass isFromModule as true.           2.2) If the value is 0, 1, or 2, pass the filterView parameter, using Location as the default option unless a specific filter view is provided in the query.          File Download Operation: After getAllFiles tool call, if user query contains \'download\', follow these steps: 1) Ask file if unspecified 2) Check allowDownload=true 3) Extract fileName, fileID, filePath. Output for downloadable files: {"file_tool_response": {"_for_pfile": "true", "_file_download_card": "true", "file_name": "fileName_from_response", "file_id": "fileID_from_response", "file_path": "filePath_from_response", "response_message": "Your [file_name] is ready - click below to download."}}.  And Strictly you should not generate download link by your own, instead you follow the `File Download Operation` procedure.  Also you have provision to generate only one file at a time, so please be specific.  To be noted the JSON you generate should stricly be valid JSON format.If the response of a particular file has fileLocationID and fileOrgStructure empty consider the file is shared with All location. In this condition show the Location as All.When a specific location file is asked include all location files too.\n\ndependencyTools: fileModulePermInitialData' },
  { tool: 'getAllODTypes', purpose: 'This tool fetches all available on-duty types configured in the organization. The response contains the list of on-duty types with their IDs and names. Use this tool before creating an on-duty request to get the applicable on-duty type ID.' },
  { tool: 'getAllRegReasons', purpose: 'This tool fetches all configured regularization reason types for the organization. The response contains a JSON array of valid reason strings. Use this tool before creating a regularization request to get the list of allowed reasons. If the response returns an empty array or no reasons, it means regularization reasons are not enforced. If reasons are returned, the user MUST use one of them. When the user provides a reason, match it to the closest reason from the returned list (handle spelling mistakes, partial matches, synonyms, or paraphrasing) and use the exact string from the list in the API call. Only ask the user to clarify if no reasonable match can be found. Present the available reasons to the user and let them choose.' },
  { tool: 'getApplicableInfo', purpose: 'Fetches the mapping of all applicable entity IDs to their names for the supported mapping types (department, location, role, designation, employeetype). Response is structured by mapping type with ID-to-name mappings. Use this to resolve any applicability IDs from other tools into human-readable names for display. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).' },
  { tool: 'getApplicablePermForUser', purpose: 'This tool fetches the applicable permission types for a specific user (employee permission requests, not admin hour-permission rules). The response is the full detailed information available for each type: IDs, names, and allowed duration limits. Use before applyPermission to resolve permissionId and when the user asks for detailed information about which permission types apply to someone  -  there is no separate detail API per type; this list is the complete source.      Pass the erecno of the user for whom applicable permissions need to be fetched.' },
  { tool: 'getApplicableShiftsForUser', purpose: 'This tool fetches the applicable shifts for a specific user that they can request to change to. The response contains the list of shifts with their IDs and names. Use this tool before creating a shift change request to get the available shift options.      Pass the erecno of the user as a JSONArray. Use current user\'s erecno if no other user is mentioned.' },
  { tool: 'getApplicableSpecificPolicy', purpose: 'Resolves the applicable specific attendance settings_id for a given employee (erecno) and optional orgday. If orgday is omitted, it resolves using the current attendance day and mapped shift for that day. Use when the user asks which specific attendance policy will be applied for an employee on a date. and then call getSpecificPolicyDetail with the resolved settings_id to show the policy details. This tool is essential for understanding which specific policy applies to an employee on a given day, especially when multiple policies exist with different applicability rules.' },
  { tool: 'getAppraisalCycles', purpose: 'Fetches the list of appraisal cycles configured in the organisation. The response includes cycle name, cycle ID (used as cycleId in other tools), cycle status, configured review types (self, multirater, appraiser), start and end dates, and applicable employee groups. Supports pagination via the following parameters: offset (int, must be greater than 0) sets the starting index of results; limit (int, range 1-200) controls the maximum number of cycles returned per request. By default set limit as 5. If neither is specified, all cycles are returned. Use this tool whenever you need to identify a specific cycle before calling getReviewStatus or any cycle-dependent action.' },
  { tool: 'getAppraisalFinalRatingsofUser', purpose: 'Fetches the final appraisal ratings of a specific employee across their last N completed appraisal cycles. The employee_erecno in the URL identifies the target employee. For the current user, use the logged-in user\'s own erecno. For any other employee, first resolve their name or employee ID to an erecno using the getEmployeeBasicDetails tool. Supports pagination via the following parameters: offset (int, must be greater than 0) sets the starting index of results; limit (int, range 1-200) controls the maximum number of cycle ratings returned. The response includes cycle name, final rating score, rating label, and review completion details for each cycle. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getApprovals', purpose: 'Retrieve approval listings and requests based on filters. Use action=\'myApprovals\' to get items pending your approval (approve/reject), or action=\'myRequests\' to get requests you have submitted. Filter approvalStatus by: pending | approved | rejected | approvedorrejected | cancelled | all. Note: \'cancelled\' applies only to action=\'myRequests\' and is not applicable to \'myApprovals\'. Optional filters include: erceno (ERECNO of the approver); servicename to restrict by module (Performance | Leavetracker | Attendance | Timetracker, etc.); and recordOwner (ERECNO of the record owner, for action=\'myApprovals\'). If servicename=\'LEAVE\', set getBasicDetails=true.' },
  { tool: 'getAttendanceDetailedReport', purpose: 'This tool can be used for fetching attendance individual dates detailed report of user.          This tool starts by fetching knowing whether data is required for all users or single user or muliple users for comparision or lising. If all user data is required then this parameter should not be passed. If specific or individual user data is required erecno of those users is required.                Response parsing when all user data is fetched         Path: result[i].employeeDetails          mail id - Employees Email ID           erecno - Employee record number - string          last name - Employee last name - string          first name - Employee first name - string          id - Employee ID - string         Path: result[i].attendanceDetails[date]          ShiftStartTime - Shift start time - string (hh:mm AM/PM)          Status - Attendance status (Present/Absent/Leave etc.) - string          paidBreakHours - Paid break hours - string (hh:mm)          unPaidBreakHours - Unpaid break hours - string (hh:mm)          FirstIn - First in-time - string (datetime or \'-\')          FirstIn_Location - Location of first in-time - string          LastOut - Last out-time - string (datetime or \'-\')          LastOut_Location - Location of last out-time - string          ShiftName - Name of the shift - string          ShiftEndTime - Shift end time - string (hh:mm AM/PM)          TotalHours - Total attendance hours - string (hh:mm)          WorkingHours - Actual working hours - string (hh:mm)          DeviationTime - Deviation from expected shift time - string (hh:mm)                  Response parsing when single user data is fetched by passing erecno parameter         Path: [date]          ShiftStartTime - Shift start time - string (hh:mm AM/PM)          Status - Attendance status - string          paidBreakHours - Paid break hours - string (hh:mm)          unPaidBreakHours - Unpaid break hours - string (hh:mm)          OverTime - Overtime hours - string (hh:mm)          FirstIn - First in-time - string (datetime or \'-\')          FirstIn_Location - Location of first in-time - string          LastOut - Last out-time - string (datetime or \'-\')          LastOut_Location - Location of last out-time - string          ShiftName - Name of the shift - string          ShiftEndTime - Shift end time - string (hh:mm AM/PM)          TotalHours - Total attendance hours - string (hh:mm)          WorkingHours - Actual working hours - string (hh:mm)' },
  { tool: 'getAttendancePolicySettings', purpose: 'Returns the organization default attendance policy for working hours and calculations. Use when the user asks about FILO versus total hours, minimum minutes for a full or half day, expected hours per day, whether weekends, holidays, or approved leaves count toward the pay period, overtime or late-night handling, or any question about rounding or grace on check-in or check-out times (including whether early check-in round-off is enabled and the configured grace minutes). Do not use getCheckinCheckoutSettings for those topics - that tool covers punch permissions and reminders only. When several scoped policies exist for different groups, list or resolve them with getSpecificPolicies and getSpecificPolicyDetail.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=policy) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]). Convert minute values to hours:minutes format.         3. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs, or record IDs to the user.         4. Resolve all referenced entities (departments, locations) using dependency tools  -  never expose raw IDs.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         DISPLAY RULES (when summarising to the user):         - Working hours: Strict mode (is_min_hours_enabled=true, use_shift_hrs=false) -> show min_hours_full_day, max_hours_halfday, min_hours_half_day; hide hours_per_day.         - Working hours: Lenient mode (is_min_hours_enabled=false) -> show hours_per_day OR use_shift_hrs note; hide min_hours_full_day / max_hours_halfday / min_hours_half_day.         - Round-off: hide all *_round_off fields when is_round_off_avail=false. When grace_period has an Intime rule, hide late_check_in_round_off; when grace_period has an Outtime rule, hide early_check_out_round_off. round_off_hours always shows (when round-off enabled) and may co-exist with grace Worktime as a stricter inner tolerance.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'getAttendanceSettingsMethods', purpose: 'Returns which attendance employee-request modules are enabled for the organization: regularization (is_regularization_enabled), permission (is_permission_enabled), on-duty (is_on_duty_enabled), break (is_break_enabled), kiosk (is_kiosk_enabled), and office-in/remote-in differential (is_office_in_remote_in_diff_enabled). Also returns is_live_location_tracking_enabled. Call this before addRegularization, addOnDuty, applyPermission, or any module-gated settings GET or update action. If the relevant flag is false, do not call the corresponding action - inform the user that the feature is disabled.         When presenting results:         1. Derive a clear English label for each param_name (e.g. is_regularization_enabled -> \'Regularization Enabled\', is_on_duty_enabled -> \'On-Duty Enabled\') and show it as: [label]  -  [value].         2. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs, or record IDs to the user.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.' },
  { tool: 'getAttendanceSettingsParams', purpose: 'Returns every configurable parameter for a given attendance settings group (mode), with each param\'s human-readable label and description.      When using the response:      ID presentation (CRITICAL - applies to every attendance settings GET and update summary): Never show any form of ID to the user unless they explicitly ask to see IDs. This includes record IDs, locId, policy_id, settings_id, permission_id, erecno, mail/template IDs, od type IDs, geo_range IDs, kiosk device IDs, leave-type IDs in grace_period, and raw param_name keys. Always resolve IDs to human-readable names using the appropriate dependency tools (getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getGeoRangeDetails, getKioskDeviceDetails, getApplicableInfo, getShiftInfo, listPermissionRules, getRemotePolicies, getSpecificPolicies, etc.). Use IDs only internally when calling APIs. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).      DISPLAY PRESENTATION (when presenting to the user): Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user - use labels and plain language only.      1. Always call this before displaying any attendance settings - map each param_name to its label and description; present values using labels and resolved entity names only (never raw IDs).      2. For org-wide settings, accepted mode values: methods, checkincheckout, policy, officeinremotein, regularization, onduty, permission, remotepolicy, report, breakpolicy, break, additionaloptions. For specific attendance policies, use mode=specificpolicy. Kiosk portal/device CRUD, live location tracking, present-by-default, and absent scheduler use dedicated tools (not this params endpoint).      3. For specific attendance policies, call mode=specificpolicy once - it returns all fields in a single call (working hour calculation, access, reminders, report access, regularization, grace_period, live_location_tracking, mail_templates). No need to call per-mode separately.      4. Working hours: is_min_hours_enabled true = strict mode (min_hours_full_day, min_hours_half_day required); false = lenient mode (hours_per_day when not using shift). is_filo true = first check-in/last check-out only; false = every valid in/out pair. use_shift_hrs derives hours from shift. show_ot_dt enables overtime and deviation calculation. is_max_hrs_enabled caps credited minutes (max_hours_fullday; max_hours_halfday strict only). All durations are in minutes.      5. Round-off fields (early_check_in_round_off, late_check_in_round_off, early_check_out_round_off, late_check_out_round_off, *_mins, round_off_hours) - adjust punch/worked times toward shift boundaries only; does NOT deduct leave (not grace period). *_round_off=true snaps all punches; *_mins=N snaps within threshold. Mutually exclusive pairs per direction.      6. Grace period (grace_period) - counts deviations and deducts leave or marks absent when limits are exceeded; does not change punch times (not round-off). Structure: {considerHighestPenalty?: boolean, rules:[...]} - rule order is processing order. Per rule: Intime = first check-in late by N minutes; Outtime = last check-out early by N minutes; Worktime / Coretime = hours short by N minutes (include only needed dimensions). graceMode 0 = penalize when count exceeds allowDays in period; 1 = penalize every Nth deviation (N=allowDays). period: 0=week, 1=month, 2=pay period. Use returned label and description when explaining to the user.      7. Access and permissions (checkincheckout / specificpolicy entry fields): web/mobile punch allowed; show_all_entries; restrict_same_source_check_out; track_location and mandatory location on web/mobile; restrict iOS assistant entries; block entries on approved leave days; show_early_late_entries (not applicable when grace period enabled); facial capture/verify on web/mobile; edit_own_entries with optional notify flags and mail; view/edit reportee entries (edit requires view). show_in_out_att_status is org general settings in UI but may appear in specific policy API.      8. Reminders (entry fields): employee check-in/out reminders (check_in_before_reminder, check_in_after_reminder, check_out_before_reminder, check_out_after_reminder - minutes before/after shift; custom templates in_remainder_*, out_remainder_*); attendance deviation alerts - missed check-in (check_in_notify_rep_man), late check-in, early check-out (manager and employee thresholds in minutes); insufficient working hours and core hours (working_hrs_notify_*, core_hrs_notify_* at shift end; manager/employee can be enabled separately). Not grace period. To disable any optional minute param above via PUT, send that param as -1 (omitting it alone does not disable under partial PUT).      9. Report access (specificpolicy report fields): is_report_view_allowed_to_manager; Expected vs worked hours report view/edit for manager and employee (show_bal_ot_perm_*, edit_bal_ot_perm_* - edit requires view); is_carry_over_ot (org UI); view preferences for managers - payable hours, paid break, unpaid break on reportee attendance views.      10. Regularization (mode=regularization or specificpolicy): is_raise_multi_reg_enabled true=new check-in/out entries kept with originals, false=replace first check-in/last check-out only; is_reg_reason_enabled + reg_reasons; is_attach_mandatory; reg_restricted_after = days from date being regularized; reg_allowed_time + reg_allowed_in_period (0=week, 1=month, 2=pay period); is_reg_allowed_for_future; is_reg_allowed_only_for_remote_work (org when remote approval enabled).      11. Office-In/Remote-In (mode=officeinremotein): punch-source toggles classify which channels count as office-in (biometric, API, kiosk+ids, IP+ip_ranges, geo+selected_geo_ranges, FTP, web import, reg/on-duty/permission entries). off_rem_consider 1-6 daily rule (3 needs office_in_threshold_hrs in minutes). is_reg_enabled/is_on_duty_enabled/is_permission_enabled here are classification sources, not org module toggles (those are on methods).      12. Hour-permission rules (mode=permission): period_type 1=week, 2=month; allowed_time_in_mins per period; allow_outside_shift false=within shift only; extend_with_grace applies when within shift only; min_time/max_time optional per-request duration caps in minutes; applicable_fields JSONObject (applicable*/exception* per dimension) when is_applicable_to_all is false.      13. On-duty (mode=onduty): duration toggles (full/half/quarter/hour); od_types {id:name} map; is_od_restricted_for_future true blocks future dates.      14. Remote work policy (mode=remotepolicy): limit_restricted+days+period (1=week, 2=month); remote_approval_type 1/2/3; applicable_for JSONObject (user/loc/dept/desg/role arrays, applicable_to_all); WFH reasons when enabled.      15. Late-night work (mode=policy only - org general policy, NOT specificpolicy): is_late_night_tracking_enabled splits worked time into regular vs late-night present/OT buckets using per-location daily windows; requires late_night_data when enabling. late_night_data: one window per location (locId, from/to as minutes from midnight, action add|edit|delete on PUT only; GET returns track_late_night_work without action). ot_outside_margin: when late-night tracking is on, hours outside shift margin are treated as OT in the split (shift margin, not a late-night margin).      16. Always use param_name (not label) when sending values in API calls - labels are for user display only.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getGeoRangeDetails, getKioskDeviceDetails, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, getShiftInfo, listPermissionRules, getRemotePolicies, getSpecificPolicies' },
  { tool: 'getAttendanceSummary', purpose: 'This tool can be used for fetching attendance summary of user like total payable days, total worked hours, total payable hours, overtime, leave, weekend, holiday days count can be optained.          This tool starts by fetching knowing whether data is required for all users or single user or muliple users for comparision or lising. If all user data is required then this parameter should not be passed. If specific or individual user data is required erecno of those users is required. For parameter erecno, erecno of users for whom tool should be invoked must be mentioned as string in comma separated formated.               From the given JSON response, navigate to summaryReport[i] (where i = index for each user). Extract only the following fields with their key names. Maintain the same JSON hierarchy. The type and meaning of each field is described below. Ignore all other fields.                deptName - Employees department name - string        emailId - Employees Email ID - string        name - User name - string        employeeId - Employee ID in profile - string        nonStatWeekend_ot - Overtime on non-statutory weekends - number (secs)        totalPaidBreakHours - Total paid break hours - string (hh:mm)        zp_HolidaySecs - Holidays in this month - number (secs)        holiday_ot - Holiday attendance - number (secs)        lateNightWorkingHours - Total late-night working hours - number (secs)        totalUnPaidBreakInSecs - Total unpaid break hours - number (secs)        totalDays - Total calendar days in the given period - number        expectedWorkingDays - Expected working days excluding weekends and holidays - number        totalWorkedDays - Worked days count - number        absentDays - Absent days count - number        weekendDays - Weekend days count - number        holidayDays - Holiday days count - number        paidLeaveDays - Paid leave days count - number        LOPDays - Loss of Pay days - number        onDutyDays - On-duty days count - number        totalPaidOffDays - Total paid off days including weekends holidays and leave - number        totalPayableDays - Total payable days - number        expectedWorkingHours - Expected working hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        totalWorkedHours - Worked hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        weekendHours - Weekend hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        holidayHours - Holiday attendance hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        paidLeaveHours - Paid leave hours - string (hh:mm)        LOPHours - Loss of Pay hours - string (hh:mm)        onDutyHours - On-duty hours - string (hh:mm)        totalPaidOffHours - Paid off hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        totalPayableHours - Payable hours - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)        overTime - Overtime hours - number secs, convert to hh:mm        deviationTime - Deviation time - number secs, convert to hh:mm        netOvertime - Total Net overtime - number (secs, convert to hh:mm)' },
  { tool: 'getAttritionReport', purpose: 'This action retrieves employee attrition data within a specified time period.             If the user requests department-wise attrition, obtain the department ID using the getDepartmentDetails tool. location-specific attrition ,first get the Location ID using getLocationDetails tool call.             If attrition is required for a specific department, send the Department ID instead of the Department Name. Avoid sending the department name in the request.             Default consider overall attrition If the user specifies department-wise or location-wise attrition, In the response, send the department name or location name instead of their IDs.             Attrition data is available only for two years - the current year and the previous year.             This tool call is only for generating Attrition reports. Do not include or send Joining reports or any other type of report.             Parameters:             mode - GRAPH(0), LIST(1) If the user specifies employee attrition records, set mode to 1. In all other cases, set mode to 0. Mode 1 retrieves only employee records for the specified month, and no reports are generated in this mode. Both horizIndex and stIndex are mandatory parameters.             intervalType - SixMonthsInterval(0), ThreeMonthsInterval(1), OneYearOneMonthInterval(3), OneYearInterval(3), QuarterlyInterval(4), TenYearsInterval(5), customDate(6),             periodCategory - RECENT(0), SPECIFIC(1) ,periodCategory defines the type of interval: 0 -> Recent Year: Covers the current month to the same month of the previous year.1 -> Specified Year: Covers the specified start month to the end month (a one-year interval based on the start date).If periodCategory is 1, the parameter specificCategVal is mandatory to define the start and end months.RULE: When periodCategory is 1, you must always send specificCategVal. Never omit it.             specificCategStMon - User-specified Start period {month:M,year:YYYY},             specificCategEnMon - User-specified End period {month:M,year:YYYY},             repType - adminReports | teamReports | myReports,             horizIndex - if periodCategory is 0, the period covers the current month to the same month of the previous year (for example, from November 2024 to November 2025). In this case, take the month index corresponding to that range - for example, if the selected month is October, its index is 11.If periodCategory is 1, the period covers the specified start month to the end month (a one-year interval based on the start date). In this case, use the month index(January(0) February(1)...November(10) December(11)) based on the given range defined by periodCategory             stIndex - record start index,start with 1,             specificCategVal - (Required if periodCategory is 1) User-specified year (YYYY),             empTypeId - Default: All Users; if specified, use the provided value. only option Id,             deptId - if particular department attrition needed send DepartmentId,              locId - if particular location attrition needed send LocationId if location Id is unavailable get it by given tool call.             groupByField - If attrition is requested for a specific department or location, send the corresponding column parameters - for department, use DEPARTMENTNAME; for location, use LOCATION. Do not send plain values like \'department\' or \'location\'.Don\'t send DepartmentId or LocationId. Get the corresponding Department or Location name from the related tool calls according to the result\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'getBenefitCategories', purpose: 'This action is used to get the list of benefit categories configured in the organization such as Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Retirement etc.' },
  { tool: 'getBenefitPlanDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific benefit plan including coverage options, contribution details, eligibility rules, and plan documents.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'getBenefitPlans', purpose: 'This action is used to get the list of benefit plans configured in the organization including plan name, plan type, category, provider, and status.' },
  { tool: 'getBreak', purpose: 'Fetches full detail of a single break definition by record_id (path). Response includes break_on_work_hrs tiers with keys breakTime and workingHrs (both minutes). When updating accrual breaks, send the same key names - do NOT rename to breakMinutes or working_hours. applicable_shifts are shift IDs - call getShiftInfo to show shift names. Resolve record_id via listBreaks.\n\ndependencyTools: listBreaks, getShiftInfo' },
  { tool: 'getBreakPolicySettings', purpose: 'Fetches break policy configuration (Settings > Break Policy): break regularization toggles (enable, add/edit entries, mandatory reason/attachment, time and count limits), missed-break alerts (notify employee, reporting manager, or specific users at shift end when a break is fully missed), and missed-break exception actions (take later, treat as overtime, or record only).' },
  { tool: 'getCaseAddSettings', purpose: 'Fetch org-level case submission settings. Always call this immediately when the user wants to raise a case - before asking any question.' },
  { tool: 'getCheckInFrequencyOptions', purpose: 'Fetches the available check-in frequency options for a given frequency type (Week or Month). Use this when adding or editing key results to get valid frequencyOption values. Requires frequencyType parameter (Week or Month).' },
  { tool: 'getCheckInPlanDates', purpose: 'Fetches the check-in plan dates for a specific key result. This is an internal dependency tool used before performing a check-in to get available planIds and their corresponding dates. Requires keyResultId.' },
  { tool: 'getCheckinCheckoutSettings', purpose: 'Returns how attendance punches may be recorded and who may change them: web and mobile punch allowance, photo and facial verification on punch, whether location is captured or required, whether employees can edit their own entries, whether managers can view or edit reportee entries, reminder windows before or after shift for check-in or check-out, deviation alerts to managers and employees (missed check-in, late check-in, early check-out), and insufficient working/core hours alerts at shift end. Use for punch-channel, edit-permission, reminder, and deviation-alert questions only. For working-hour round-off, grace rounding, FILO, minimum hours, or pay-period rules, use getAttendancePolicySettings instead.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=checkincheckout) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]).         3. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs, or record IDs to the user.         4. Resolve all referenced entities using dependency tools  -  never expose raw IDs.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams' },
  { tool: 'getCheckinHistory', purpose: 'Fetches the check-in history for a specific key result showing all past progress updates. Requires keyResultId (long).' },
  { tool: 'getClientDetails', purpose: 'Retrieve the details of a specific client using the clientId.' },
  { tool: 'getClients', purpose: 'This action is to get clients. assignedTo is user by default current user or set of user for whom clients need to be fetched given as comma seperated erecno. isFromFilter and includeDeptClients are always sent as true to fetch clients assigned to user. searchKey is used to search for specific clients.' },
  { tool: 'getCompletedTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks marked as \'Completed\' from the user\'s task list.' },
  { tool: 'getCompoffRecords', purpose: 'Fetches compensatory off (comp-off) requests (GET /api/v3/leave-tracker/compensatory). When filtering by person, department, or location name, resolve to IDs via dependency tools first; never invent IDs. For self, CURRENTUSER erecno is enough without getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'getCurrentlyRunningTimer', purpose: 'This API retrieves the currently running timer information.' },
  { tool: 'getCycleRatingEmployees', purpose: 'Fetches employees for a selected rating bucket in an appraisal cycle. Pass exactly one filter: either type or rating_id. type supports max (Best Performer of a Cycle) and min (Low Performer of a Cycle). rating_id must be taken from getRatingSummaryOfCycle when fetching employees for a specific rating. Pagination is mandatory through offset and limit, and limit must not exceed 10 records per call.\n\ndependencyTools: getAppraisalCycles, getRatingSummaryOfCycle' },
  { tool: 'getDepartmentDetails', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch department basic details such as lead/head,parent department of a department,count of members in a department.Get department name as input and pass it value to searchText param.Make sure the department name is correct from the department list given in the prompt.Strictly use this tool when basic department details are needed and data is fetched based on department name. STRICT COUNT EXCLUSION: Do not use this tool for employee count, headcount, or employees/users tagged-under queries, even if the user mentions a department-like name. For those queries, resolve the matching Employee form field/options and use getRecordCount only.' },
  { tool: 'getDepartmentObjectives', purpose: 'Fetches department-level objectives. Requires sIndx (start index), startPeriod and endPeriod (date range), okrStatus (status filter). Optional: departmentId (from getOkrDepartments), approvalStatus (-1=Pending, 0=Rejected, 1=Approved, 2=All). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getOkrDepartments].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getOkrDepartments' },
  { tool: 'getDepartmentShiftGrouping', purpose: 'Fetch shift-wise grouped employees for a department or reportees on a single date.                  Key Features:         - Get shift-wise employee details grouped by shift         - Display results in a structured table format per shift         - Shift employee count = size of that shift\'s employee array         - If a specific employee count for a particular shift is requested, return that shift\'s array size         - Report count available when filterMode=members         - Total grouped employee count available in employeeCount         - Supports single date only (defaults to current date)                  Parameters:         - filterMode (mandatory):              \'members\' = Department members             \'reportees\' = Current user\'s reportees         - dataSelect (optional, only if filterMode=reportees):             1 = Direct reportees (default)             2 = All reportees         - customDate (optional): dd-MMM-yyyy (defaults to current date)         - departmentId (optional): Applicable only if filterMode=members (defaults to current user\'s department). Resolve via getDepartmentDetails if not provided.                  Response:         Path: result.data         - shiftInfo -> Shift metadata (shiftName, fTime, tTime, colorCode)         - shiftWiseEmployeesList -> Employees grouped by shiftId         - employeeCount -> Total grouped employees         - all / direct -> Reportee count details' },
  { tool: 'getDependentDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific dependent.\n\ndependencyTools: getDependents' },
  { tool: 'getDependents', purpose: 'This action is used to get the list of dependents configured for benefits.' },
  { tool: 'getDeptStreamHead', purpose: 'Retrieves the current stream head assigned to a specific stream within a department. Resolve $departmentId$ via getDepartmentDetails and $streamId$ via getStreamOptions before invoking; never fabricate ids.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getStreamOptions' },
  { tool: 'getDivisions', purpose: 'Retrieves a list of all divisions in the organization structure. Supports pagination via \'offset\' (1-based page number, default 1) and \'limit\' (records per page, 1-200, default 200). Use the \'is_tagged\' parameter to filter: 1 = divisions tagged in the hierarchy tree (have entries in OrgStructureMapping), 0 = divisions not tagged. Only active, non-dummy records are returned. Divisions support nesting - a division can be a child of another division. IMPORTANT: If the user refers to Divisions using a custom display name (as specified in the system prompt), use this tool - do NOT use any other tool such as getAllFiles or getRecords.' },
  { tool: 'getEarlyLateCheckInData', purpose: 'This tool can be used for fetching early late details of an employee. This data can be used to decide whether users are regularly late to office/on time to work.     This tool starts by fetching erecno of user. For parameter erecno, erecno of user for whom tool should be invoked must be mentioned as Long JsonArray. JSONArray format is only for erecno parameter.           From the JSON, go to report.empDetails which contains a nested array. Loop through each object in the innermost array. For each object:      - dateStr - Date      - shiftId - match with report.shiftDetails to get shiftName      - firstIn - First Check-In      - lastOut - Last Check-Out (if missing, keep blank)      - earlyLateComeTime - convert seconds to hh:mm; if negative, mark as \'Late by hh:mm\', if positive, mark as \'Early by hh:mm\'      - earlyLateLeaveTime - convert seconds to hh:mm; if negative, mark as \'Left Early by hh:mm\', if positive, mark as \'Worked Extra by hh:mm\'      Output format:      Date: dateStr | Shift: shiftName | First In: firstIn | Last Out: lastOut or blank | Check In Status (Mention converted earlyLateComeTime) | Check Out Status (Mention converted earlyLateLeaveTime)' },
  { tool: 'getEligibleUsersForPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch the list of all eligible users for a specific benefit plan and plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans, getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'getEmployeeBasicDetails', purpose: 'STRICT COUNT EXCLUSION: Do not use this tool for employee count, headcount, or employees/users tagged-under queries. For those requests, use getRecordCount on the employee form only after resolving the matching Employee form field/options. STRICT FORM-FIELD EXCLUSION: Do not use this tool to answer exact, full, custom, or org-specific employee form-field queries when the requested field is not one of this tool\'s basic response fields. Use the Forms flow on the employee form, fetch getFields, and retrieve the exact requested field; if the exact field/form is unclear, ask the user to choose from matching display names. This is the FIRST-CHOICE (primary) tool for employee discovery/listing. Whenever the user asks to search, get, find, list, or fetch employee(s) by name, employee id/erecno, department name, or designation/job title, you MUST try this tool first for employee basic details (do not use other tools for employee lookup for the fields specified). This also applies to bulk employee listing requests with no specific filters: call this tool and paginate using sIndex and limit until enough results are shown or the user stops. If this tool fails (error/timeout/repeated empty results that contradict the user request), then use the Forms flow as fallback: use `getRecords` for the Employee system form (formLinkName=`employee`), calling `getFields` only if you need field labelnames, and then fetch via `getRecords` with required fields and pagination. This action returns only basic employee fields such as name, email, erecNo, employeeId, zuid, department name/id, designation, contact details (mobile/extension), availability, photo and reporting manager details, and supports search by name, department, designation, or erecno; before calling the action compare the user input against both the department and designation lists and if the term matches both or no clear match exists ask the user to clarify which filter should be applied. When a search by name returns multiple employees, auto-select using the following strict priority order: 1) Direct Reportees or Direct Manager of the current user, 2) Same Department, 3) Same Designation, 4) Same Work Location, 5) Same Role. Do not ask upfront; if multiple candidates tie at the highest-ranked criterion, select the first result returned and proceed. After completing the desired action of user query, inform the user that other employees with the same name exist and offer a simple switch option. If an explicit erecno/employeeId or zpu token is provided, prefer it over name search. LOCATION RESOLUTION RULE (STRICT): Never show a raw location id to the user. If the employee response contains location ids, call `getLocationDetails` once with all ids batched in `locationIds` and display the resolved name. If a name string is already present, use it as-is. If resolution fails, omit the location field instead of showing the id. FALLBACK (STRICT - NO EXCEPTIONS): If this tool returns an error/failure OR the user requests employee data fields that are NOT returned by this tool OR no record is found OR totalRecords=0 OR error 7040 (Permission denied) - do NOT emit any \'not found\' or error response or permission denied. In all these cases the employee or the requested field may still exist in the system. Reasons this tool may miss an existing employee include: scope or permission restrictions, search by first name only (e.g. \'John\'), search by unsupported attributes (e.g. nickname, custom fields), or partial name mismatches. MANDATORY next steps: (1) call getFields with formLinkName=\'employee\' to get the exact label name for the user\'s search attribute and requested field, (2) call getRecords with formLinkName=\'employee\', searchParams built using RECORD_FILTER rules with those label names and the user\'s original search value, and fields including the requested output fields. If getRecords returns records, present them. If getRecords returns empty, it will automatically call GetFormRecordsAcrossViews. If GetFormRecordsAcrossViews also returns no records, ONLY THEN say the employee was not found and ask the user whether to search among inactive or exited employees; upon confirmation use getRecords on the employee form with employeeType=inactive and appropriate search filters. EXIT/OFFBOARDED RULE: If the query is explicitly about exit details, exit form, or already offboarded employees, do NOT use getEmployeeBasicDetails at all; directly use getRecords on the employee form with employeeType=inactive and search filters (resolve field names via getFields). Use this tool only if the user request can be satisfied using the basic employee fields returned by this action; if any other employee details are required, do not use this tool and check other employee tools or the full employee form instead.' },
  { tool: 'getEmployeeBenefitPlans', purpose: 'Fetches the benefit plans (medical, dental, vision, life insurance, retirement, HSA/FSA, etc.) that an employee is currently enrolled in for a given plan year. This is the primary action for viewing enrolled plan details.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks \'show my plans\', \'show my benefits\', \'what insurance am I enrolled in\', \'show my current coverage\', \'my benefit plans for this year\', or \'view my elections\', use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s enrolled plans (\'show John\'s benefits\', \'what plans is employee X enrolled in\', \'list enrolled plan details for employee Y\'), first resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails, then use that erecno. Admins can view any employee\'s enrolled plans. Non-admins can view plans of employees they have access to (e.g., reportees).      STRICT (MANDATORY CHAINING): You MUST call getUserPlanYears FIRST (with the same erecno) and obtain a plan year ID. Then invoke getEmployeeBenefitPlans with filterData containing the plan_years array. Always pass filterData as a request parameter: filterData={"offset":1,"plan_years":["$planYearId$"]}. Replace $planYearId$ with the plan_year_id obtained from getUserPlanYears (pick the one with is_current=true if the user did not specify a year). NEVER call this action without filterData.plan_years populated - the API returns an empty result without it, which means the employee has NO enrolled plans for that year, NOT a configuration error.      Returns plan-level details: plan name, provider, coverage type, enrollment status, total contributions, employee and employer contribution amounts, coverage tier, and dependents covered.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserPlanYears, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getEmployeePayCycle', purpose: 'Use when Loss of Pay (LOP) or any flow needs the pay period setting and pay cycle dates for a specific employee. Resolve employee via getEmployeeBasicDetails (CURRENTUSER erecno for self). Always ask whether they want the current pay cycle or previous pay cycle; if they do not choose, use previous (cycle_offset=-1). Pass cycle_offset=0 for current, cycle_offset=-1 for previous. Returns pay_period_setting_id, from_date, and to_date to pass into getLOPReport. Do not invent pay period setting ids or dates.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getEmployeeShiftDetails', purpose: 'Fetch employee shift details for a given date range using employee, department, or location filters.         Parameters:         - erecno (optional): Comma-separated Erecno(s)         - departmentId (optional): Department ID (resolve via getDepartmentDetails)         - locationId (optional): Location ID (resolve via getLocationDetails)         - sDate, eDate (optional): dd-MMM-yyyy (default: today)                  If no filter is provided, shift details for all employees will be fetched.                  Response: result.data (Array)         Includes empId, empname (sanitize), emailId, deptId, locId, and date-wise shiftList.                  Each shift:         shiftName, ftime, ttime (convert to HH:mm), isWeekend.                  Present the data as a table with the following structure:          the first column is the employee (e.g. name and/or email), and the remaining columns are one per date in the range.         Do not use HTML tags such as br for line breaks. Use plain text formatting or actual line breaks only. Do not output br as text.         In each date cell, show the shift as the shift name plus the time range in HH:mm-HH:mm, and add "Weekend" when the shift is on a weekend.          If an employee has more than one shift on a date, use a separate row for each shift for that employee.          When there are no matching records, show the message: "No shift details found for selected filters\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'getEmployeesWithoutKRAs', purpose: 'Returns the list of employees within the caller\'s scope (self plus reportees for non-admins, all visible employees for admins) who currently have no KRAs tagged in the Performance module. Supports pagination via offset (int, must be greater than or equal to 0) and limit (int, range 1-200, default 200). By default set limit as 5. Response is the standard EntityCRUD employees record shape: extract erecno and the basic employee display fields (first name, last name, employee id, department, designation) per record. Use this tool when the user asks \'who has no KRAs\', \'employees without KRAs\', \'list employees with KRAs pending\', or any equivalent phrasing about identifying employees pending KRA assignment.' },
  { tool: 'getEnrollmentDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific benefit enrollment including coverage selection, dependents covered, contribution breakdown, and enrollment dates.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollments' },
  { tool: 'getEnrollmentStats', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch enrollment statistics for a specific benefit plan and plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans, getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'getEnrollmentWindowDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific enrollment window.\n\ndependencyTools: getEnrollmentWindows' },
  { tool: 'getEnrollmentWindows', purpose: 'This action is used to get the list of enrollment windows configured in the organization.' },
  { tool: 'getEntities', purpose: 'Retrieves a list of all legal entities in the organization structure. Supports pagination via \'offset\' (1-based page number, default 1) and \'limit\' (records per page, 1-200, default 200). Use the \'is_tagged\' parameter to filter: 1 = entities tagged (placed) in the hierarchy tree, 0 = entities not tagged. Only active, non-dummy records are returned. IMPORTANT: If the user refers to Legal Entities using a custom display name (as specified in the system prompt), use this tool - do NOT use any other tool such as getAllFiles or getRecords.' },
  { tool: 'getFeedback', purpose: 'Fetches feedback details for a given employee. fbmode is mandatory and accepts: myreview (logged-in user own perspective, further filtered by submode) or myteam (feedbacks received by the specified userErecNo). submode is applicable only when fbmode=myreview and accepts: givenfbs_tome (feedbacks received by me), givenfbs_byme (feedbacks I gave to others), subordinatesfbs (feedbacks received by my direct reportees), allfbs (all three combined). userErecNo is the target employee erecNo; defaults to the logged-in user if omitted. fbtypeId filters by feedback category ID from getFeedbackCategories; default is -1 (all types). configId is the appraisal cycle ID used for reviewer-based access check. periodStatus filters by date range (1=all time, 2-7 for specific periods). Always send isTypesNeeded=true to include feedback category metadata, per-type counts, and anonymous feedback setting in the response, unless the user explicitly says it is not needed.' },
  { tool: 'getFeedbackCategories', purpose: 'This is action is used to fetch Feedback categories that is available in the Feedback module in Performance.' },
  { tool: 'getFieldOptions', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch available options for non-lookup form fields (Picklist, Dropdown, Gender, BloodGroup, etc.). For Lookup fields, use getLookupOptions instead. It uses the formlinkname from the `identifyForm` response and the field list from the `getFields` response. MANDATORY: optionsNeededFields is required when calling this action; do not invoke without it. STRICT: optionsNeededFields must contain only labelname values from the getFields response (never display names or other identifiers). From the getFields response, identify non-lookup fields and pass their labelname values as a comma-separated string (e.g. optionsNeededFields=Status,Location). Always send includeOptions=true in parameters. Only request options for fields you actually need to keep the response small.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm' },
  { tool: 'getFields', purpose: 'This action is used to find the formlinkname from the `identifyForm` response and obtain the corresponding field list.      FIELD AVAILABILITY RULE: After fetching fields, if the user requests to filter by a field that does not exist in the getFields response,      inform them that the requested field is not available for filtering.      Offer to show the list of available fields they can query and suggest alternative fields that may help achieve their intended filter results.     PARAM USAGE: When calling this tool as a dependency of `getRecords` (filtering or viewing), pass onlyEditableFields=false to include all fields the user can view, not just fields with edit permission; otherwise by default only fields with role-based edit permission are returned.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getFieldOptions, getLookupOptions, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'getFormConfigurations', purpose: 'Internal helper - retrieves view type permissions and filter configuration for a form. Used by GetFormRecordsAcrossViews to determine which view types are accessible before fetching records across views.' },
  { tool: 'getFormView', purpose: 'This action is used to find the form ID from the `identifyForm` response and get the default views\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm' },
  { tool: 'getGeoRangeDetails', purpose: 'Fetches geo range details used in attendance Office-In/Remote-In setup. Each geo range includes geo_range_id, geo_range_name, and map_values. Use this to resolve selected_geo_ranges ids before creating or updating office-in/remote-in settings.' },
  { tool: 'getGoalsCountReport', purpose: 'Fetches the Goals Count report under Performance Appraisal Reports. Returns aggregated goal counts. Parameter usage: managerId is the erecno of the manager whose team is being viewed; leave empty when scope is adminReports. from and to define the period in Organisation date format strictly follow the date format or else ask the user and default to the first and last day of the current month when the user does not specify a range. sIndex is offset , default value is 1 and returns up to 20 records per , mention that the result is for 20 records , for next records add 20 in sIndex as 21 , for another next 41 and so on. employeeStatus must always be sent as [19] (default value); do not change this value unless the user explicitly requests otherwise. repType must be \'adminReports\' as default value , otherwise \'teamReports\' (manager fetching their team\'s data). status must always be sent as [19] (default value),do not change this value unless the user explicitly requests otherwise ; leave empty if the user does not specify. dateType is a JSON array describing which date the from/to range applies to: 0=Created Date, 1=Start Date, 2=Completed Date, 3=Due Date; defaults to an empty array when the user does not specify. The employeeArr/locationArr/departmentArr/entityArr/businessUnitArr/divisionArr/designationArr filters are not used by this tool. Show the user suggestion that this is 20 records fetched , ask user for next fetch until last fetch is less than 20 records' },
  { tool: 'getHighPriorityTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks classified as \'High\' priority from the user\'s task list' },
  { tool: 'getJobDetails', purpose: 'Retrieve detailed information about a specific job using the jobId.' },
  { tool: 'getJobSchedule', purpose: 'This action is to get the list of job schedules add for the user or the user repotees scheduled for a period to work on jobs in that period, fromDate will be start of period and toDate will be end of period in yyyy-MM-dd format, dateFormat default value is yyyy-MM-dd, user can be single user or multiple user with comma separated or all to get all users schedulers default is current user' },
  { tool: 'getJobs', purpose: 'This action is to get jobs. assignedTo is the user for whom the jobs are assigned default current user erecno will be used, assignedTo can be single user or multiple user with comma separated or all to get all users jobs. jobStatus is either all or in-progress or completed default value is in-progress to get in-progress jobs. projectId is id of projects with comma separated to get jobs of selected projects. searchJobName is used to search job with job name and searchJobKey specify the type of search with any of the values all, equal, notEqual, startsWith, endsWith, contains, notContains and is send if searchJobName key is sent. once jobs are fetched show them in table format with serial number. To add a job use addRecord tool with formLinkName P_TimesheetJob.' },
  { tool: 'getKeyResultDetails', purpose: 'Fetches detailed information for a specific key result. Requires keyResultId (long). Returns complete key result data including progress, owners, and check-in details.' },
  { tool: 'getKioskConfig', purpose: 'Fetches the organization-level Kiosk portal setup (Settings > Kiosk). Returns kiosk_name and portal_link when a portal exists; both are omitted when no portal has been created. Whether Kiosk check-in/out is enabled org-wide is is_kiosk_enabled from getAttendanceSettingsMethods - not returned here. For kiosk device login credentials, call getKioskLoginUsers.' },
  { tool: 'getKioskLoginUsers', purpose: 'Lists Kiosk device login credentials (Settings > Kiosk). Response: { login_users: [{ device_id, email, device_name, country, country_code, timezone, language, language_code, is_delete_captured_image_enabled }] }. Returns an empty list when no kiosk portal or devices exist. device_id is used in update/delete/password URLs.' },
  { tool: 'getKraGoals', purpose: 'Fetches the goals mapped to given KRAs for a specific employee. The kra_ids parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA IDs. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras].\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras' },
  { tool: 'getLOPReport', purpose: 'Use when the user asks for the Loss of Pay (LOP) report / unpaid leave deduction report for a pay period. Do not use for leave-type balance summary (getLeaveTypeSummaryReport), applied leave listing (getLeaveRecords), or leave balance.      Always ask whether the report is for the current pay cycle or the previous pay cycle; if the user does not choose, default to previous.      Resolve the employee first (self = CURRENTUSER erecno; otherwise getEmployeeBasicDetails). Call getEmployeePayCycle for that employee with cycle_offset=0 (current) or -1 (previous, default). Pass the returned pay_period_setting_id as pay_period_setting_Id, and from_date/to_date from the same response. Include employee_zoho_ids when scoping to that employee. Never invent setting ids or dates.      When the LOP total is non-zero for an employee (or the user asks what the LOP is made of), also call getLOPSummary for the same employee and cycle_offset, then present the leave-type breakdown (e.g. Absent 1, Sick Leave 1 totaling 2).\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeePayCycle, getLOPSummary, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getLOPSummary', purpose: 'Use when the user needs a leave-type breakdown of Loss of Pay for one employee (e.g. total LOP 2 explained as Absent 1 and Sick Leave 1). Returns lop_break_down_list with per leave type name and lop count for days/hours. Resolve employee via getEmployeeBasicDetails (CURRENTUSER for self). Pass cycle_offset=-1 (previous, default) or 0 (current); the API resolves the pay cycle server-side - do not require getEmployeePayCycle for this tool (that tool is only needed when getLOPReport needs pay_period_setting_id and from/to). When used together with getLOPReport, use the same cycle_offset. Do not use getLOPReport alone when a per-leave-type LOP explanation is needed.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getLeastProjectUsers', purpose: 'This action is to get least or less performing users for a project. projectId can be taken from the tool getProjects  by setting the param assignedTo as all and searchProjectName with name and searchProjectKey with contains. The result contains totalHours key in minutes, convert them to hours and display.\n\ndependencyTools: getProjects' },
  { tool: 'getLeaveBalance', purpose: 'This tool is used to fetch leave balance information. Do not reuse the last fetched response if it was for a different user, different year and a successful applyLeave tool call has occurred after the last fetch. Always determine from the user\'s query whose leave balance is being requested and pass the appropriate erecno: use the user\'s own erecno when they are requesting their own leave balance, the reportee\'s erecno when requesting for a reportee, and the requested user\'s erecno when an admin is requesting for others. The year parameter must be passed as a relative value, where 0 represents the current year, 1 represents the next year, -1 the previous year, -2 two years back, and so on. If the user mentions a specific date or year, calculate and pass the corresponding relative year value; if no date is mentioned, default to 0 (current year). If the user provides a date range where the start date falls in one year and the end date falls in another year, always fetch the current year leave balance. In the future, only the next year (1) is allowed, and in the past, only up to three years back is allowed (-1, -2, -3).If the leave type has doNotDisplayBalance set to true or the available key is missing, skip displaying the available balance.' },
  { tool: 'getLeaveGrants', purpose: 'Use when the user asks to view, list, find, or check leave grant / leave credit grant requests (pending, approved, or history) for self, reportees, or others. Do not use for applying leave, viewing leave records, or leave balance. When filtering by person, department, location, or leave type name, resolve to IDs via dependency tools first; never invent IDs. For self, CURRENTUSER erecno is enough without getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'getLeaveRecords', purpose: 'Use when the user asks to view, list, or find leave requests/records (applied leaves) for self, reportees, or others in a date range - including by status or leave type. Do not use for leave balance (getLeaveBalance/bookedAndBalance), leave grants (getLeaveGrants), holidays (listholidays), or leave-type summary report. When filtering by person, department, location, or leave type name, resolve to IDs via dependency tools first; never invent IDs. For self, CURRENTUSER erecno is enough without getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'getLeaveTypeSummaryReport', purpose: 'Use when the user asks for a leave type-wise summary or usage report for one specific leave type over a period (e.g. Casual Leave summary for Jan-Mar): per-employee opening_balance, closing_balance, granted, booked, lapsed, encashed, and lop. Do not use for all-leave-type booked vs balance (bookedAndBalance), applied leave listing (getLeaveRecords), or LOP payroll report (getLOPReport). Resolve leave type name to leave_type_id via fetchLeaveTypes; never invent IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'getLiveLocationTrackingSettings', purpose: 'Returns org-level live location tracking settings (Settings > Location Tracking): enabled flag, capture interval, auto checkout on capture failure, and two separate notification groups. (1) Location capture failure: notify employee, reporting manager, or specific users when the mobile app cannot capture GPS at the scheduled interval (is_notify_employee, is_notify_reporting_manager, is_notify_specific_users and template IDs). (2) Out of geo range: notify when GPS is captured successfully but falls outside the assigned geo-restricted range (is_notify_not_in_geo_* params and template IDs). Requires is_live_location_tracking_enabled=true from getAttendanceSettingsMethods before enabling.      DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show raw param names or JSON structures to the user - present values using plain language labels.' },
  { tool: 'getLocationDetails', purpose: 'This action retrieves location details such as location ID, name, country, mail alias, description, state code, and address.' },
  { tool: 'getLocationObjectives', purpose: 'Fetches location-level objectives. Requires sIndx (start index), startPeriod and endPeriod (date range), okrStatus (status filter). Optional: locationId (from getOkrLocations), approvalStatus (-1=Pending, 0=Rejected, 1=Approved, 2=All). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getOkrLocations].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getOkrLocations' },
  { tool: 'getLookupOptions', purpose: 'This action fetches available options specifically for Lookup fields. Use the formlinkname from the `identifyForm` response and the field list from the `getFields` response. MANDATORY: fields parameter is required as a JSONArray of labelname values where comptype is Lookup from the getFields response (e.g. fields=["Department","Location"]). Pass only Lookup field labelnames. Optionally pass searchtxt to filter lookup options by search text.      RESPONSE FORMAT: The response contains a lookupOptions object where each key is a field labelname and its value is an array of option objects. Each option has Value (display text) and Id (the identifier to send). Example: lookupOptions: { "FieldLabel": [ { "Value": "Option Text", "Id": "123" }, ... ] }. Match the user\'s text against the Value field and send the corresponding Id in inputData. NEVER send the Value string as inputData for Lookup fields.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getFields' },
  { tool: 'getMailMergeTemplates', purpose: '# Mail Merge Tool List Mail Merge templates and emit a download card for one.  This is a single-tool flow. No separate \'generate\' or \'download\' tool exists. After this tool returns, YOU emit the download card JSON yourself (Output Mode 2). Do not call any other tool to produce the download.  Flow: call this tool -> accumulate all pages -> match user request against active templates -> resolve recordId -> emit exactly one of the 4 Output modes.  Triggers: mail merge, mm template, generate/download document, download link, offer/experience/relieving/appointment letter, address proof, personalized document.  ## Params (both mandatory) - startInd (required): 1 first call; repeat with startInd += limit while templateDetails.length == limit. - limit (required): 200.  ## Response (top-level) - templateDetails[]: template objects. Use only isActive == 1; skip the rest silently. - employeeFormId: org Employee form ID. - Permission, fileSettings, allemplookupDetails, mmtemplatesCount: ignore.  ## Per-template fields - tid: template DB ID; maps to templateId in the card. - formId, formName: target form id and display name. - document_name: display name. May contain merge tokens like ${FirstName}; render as-is, never substitute/strip. - fname: original filename, often opaque (e.g. cnwkdcn). Fallback only when document_name is empty. - rid: Writer doc hash. NOT recordId. Never echo, never use as recordId. - url: live Writer link. Never echo, never construct. - type, isActive, DELETEDTIME, docNameList: do not surface.  ## CRITICAL rid is NOT recordId. recordId is the merge target - an employee erecno or a record in the template\'s own form. Putting rid in recordId breaks the download.  ## Match priority document_name, then fname, then formName.  ## Resolve recordId by formId If formId == employeeFormId (Employee template):   1. zpu[erecno:VALUE]zpu marker in user msg -> use VALUE.   2. User says \'me\'/\'my\'/\'I\' -> current user\'s erecno from CURRENTUSER.   3. User names another employee -> resolve via getEmployeeBasicDetails. Else (Department, Address Proof, any non-Employee form):   recordId is a record in the template\'s OWN form (formId/formName above).   1. If the user identified it (e.g. \'address proof for Engineering dept\'), resolve via getRecords for that form (use identifyForm first if you don\'t already know its formLinkName).   2. Otherwise ask once: \'Which [formName] record?\' and stop.  ## Output - exactly one mode 1. List (\'list/show/display\' templates): one line per active template as document_name (formName), grouped by formName; fall back to fname if document_name is empty. If templateDetails is empty -> \'No mail merge templates are configured.\' 2. Download (single template chosen): emit ONLY this JSON, nothing else. No prose, no code fences, no single quotes. Output must be valid JSON (JSON.parse must succeed): {"file_tool_response": {"_for_mm": true, "_file_download_card": true, "recordId": "RECORD_ID", "templateId": "TEMPLATE_ID", "formId": "FORM_ID", "file_name": "DOCUMENT_NAME_OR_FNAME", "response_message": "Your [file_name] is ready - click below to download."}} 3. Multiple matches: list candidates as document_name (formName) and ask the user to choose; do NOT auto-pick. 4. Templates exist but none matches the user\'s request: \'No template named [name] was found.\'  ## Never Put rid in recordId. Use rid, a plain name, or the current user\'s erecno as recordId for non-Employee templates. Echo url/rid/https links. Wrap Mode 2 JSON in prose. Construct download URLs manually.' },
  { tool: 'getMyObjectives', purpose: 'Fetches the current user\'s objectives. Requires sIndx (start index, integer), startPeriod and endPeriod (date range), okrStatus (status filter from getOkrStatusData), and subMode (own|contribute|keyresults). Optional: approvalStatus (-1=Pending, 0=Rejected, 1=Approved, 2=All). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData' },
  { tool: 'getMySharedFiles', purpose: 'This action retrieves shared with me files for listing using default values: fileType=0, start=0, limit=100, fileSortByType=3, isFileSortDesc=true. fileType (0) defines file type, start sets fetch index, and limit caps results. filterView is used to filter files based on searchFileName (no special chars, max 250) . fromDate/toDate set date range. fileSortByType (1-name, 2-created, 3-modified) and isFileSortDesc (true=desc) control sorting. longitude/latitude allow location-based filtering.                                                  Before invoking this tool:                                                 1) Strictly call fileModulePermInitialData to retrieve the user\'s permissions for the Employee Files module.                                                 2) From the response, read the hasEmpFileAccess parameter:                                                      2.1) pass isFromModule as true.                                                      2.2) If the hasEmpFileAccess value is 0, give No permission and exit the flow.                                                      2.3) If the hasEmpFileAccess value is 1 pass the values: fileType=0,start=0, limit=100,fileSortByType=3,isFileSortDesc=true,filterBy=my.fileType (0) defines file type, start sets fetch index, and limit caps results.                                                 File Download Operation: After getMyFiles tool call, if user query contains \'download\', follow these steps: 1) Ask file if unspecified 2) Check allowDownload=true 3) Extract fileName, fileID, filePath. Output for downloadable files: {"file_tool_response": {"_for_pfile": "true", "_file_download_card": "true", "file_name": "fileName_from_response", "file_id": "fileID_from_response", "file_path": "filePath_from_response", "response_message": "Your [file_name] is ready - click below to download."}}.  And Strictly you should not generate download link by your own, instead you follow the `File Download Operation` procedure.  Also you have provision to generate only one file at a time, so please be specific.  To be noted the JSON you generate should stricly be valid JSON format.\n\ndependencyTools: fileModulePermInitialData' },
  { tool: 'getMyTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves various tasks related to users based on filter criteria. By default, applying the filter \'my\' returns tasks assigned only to the current user. When using the filter \'all\', it returns tasks assigned to the user, tasks created by the user, unassigned tasks available for picking, and tasks belonging to the user\'s subordinates.        To retrieve tasks for users other than the current user, use the \'all\' filter and provide the employee record number (erecno) of the desired user in the \'taskOwnerErecnos\' parameter. Tasks can be filtered by status - including alltasks (0), unassigned (-1), open (1), and completed (2) - as well as by priority including alltasks(0),high(1),moderate(2),low(3), task name, and form name.         If no status is specified, tasks with an \'Open\' status are returned by default' },
  { tool: 'getObjectiveDetails', purpose: 'Fetches detailed information for a specific objective. Requires objectiveId (long). Returns complete objective data including key results, progress, and alignment info.' },
  { tool: 'getObjectiveForAlign', purpose: 'Fetches objectives available for alignment. Requires objectiveId (long), objectiveType (DEPARTMENT or ORG), and startIndex (int). Returns a list of objectives that the given objective can be aligned to.' },
  { tool: 'getOfficeInRemoteInSettings', purpose: 'Fetches the Office-In / Remote-In differentiation settings for attendance. Use this tool when the user asks about office vs remote attendance tracking, how office-in or remote-in status is determined, kiosk device configuration, IP range restrictions, geo-range/geo-fence settings, or which attendance methods are classified as office or remote.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=officeinremotein) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]). Convert minute values where applicable.         3. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs, or record IDs to the user.         4. Resolve all referenced entities using dependency tools  -  never expose raw IDs.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams' },
  { tool: 'getOkrConfigData', purpose: 'Fetches configuration data for the OKR module including period settings, weightage settings, and approval configurations. This is an internal dependency tool used before adding objectives or key results.' },
  { tool: 'getOkrDepartments', purpose: 'Fetches all departments available in the OKR module. Use this to get departmentId values needed for department-level objective operations.' },
  { tool: 'getOkrLocations', purpose: 'Fetches all locations available in the OKR module. Use this to get locationId values needed for location-level objective operations.' },
  { tool: 'getOkrStatusData', purpose: 'Fetches OKR status data including available status options for objectives. Use this to get the valid okrStatus values for filtering objectives.' },
  { tool: 'getOnDutySettings', purpose: 'Fetches on-duty configuration. Use when the user asks about how on-duty is set up, whether it is enabled, what on-duty types exist, whether reasons are mandatory, whether half-day or hourly requests are allowed, or approval rules. Distinct from getAllODTypes (simple employee-facing list).         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=onduty) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]).         3. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs (including od_type IDs), or record IDs to the user  -  show type names only.         4. Resolve all referenced entities using dependency tools  -  never expose raw IDs.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams' },
  { tool: 'getOpenTaskCount', purpose: 'This action retrieves the count of open tasks along with employee details, based on the filter (all or my). By default, filterBy=my returns the count of open tasks assigned to the current user. If filterBy=all is specified, it returns the count of open tasks for all employees.overdueBy refers to the number of days a task has extended beyond its due date while status still remaining open.' },
  { tool: 'getOrgCompetencies', purpose: 'Fetches the list of competencies configured at the organisation level. Use when the user asks about org-level competencies.' },
  { tool: 'getOrgKras', purpose: 'Fetches the list of KRAs configured at the organisation level. Use when the user asks about org-level KRAs. In response show type key represents 0 as Organisation KRA , 2 as User KRA. By default set limit as 5.' },
  { tool: 'getOrgObjectives', purpose: 'Fetches organization-level objectives. Requires sIndx (start index), startPeriod and endPeriod (date range), okrStatus (status filter). Optional: approvalStatus (-1=Pending, 0=Rejected, 1=Approved, 2=All). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData' },
  { tool: 'getOrgReviewQuestions', purpose: 'Fetches the list of review questions configured at the organisation level. Use when the user asks about review questions in the org. By default set limit as 5.' },
  { tool: 'getOrgSkills', purpose: 'Fetches the list of skills configured at the organisation level. Use when the user asks about org-level skills. By default set limit as 5.' },
  { tool: 'getOverDueTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks that are overdue, i.e., tasks where the current date has passed the due date without completion' },
  { tool: 'getParentKeyResults', purpose: 'Fetches parent-level key results for a specific objective. Requires objectiveId (long), owner (employee erecno, long), and objectivePage (MY|TEAM|DEPARTMENT|LOCATION|ORG). Dependencies: [getObjectiveDetails].\n\ndependencyTools: getObjectiveDetails' },
  { tool: 'getPendingTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks with an \'Open\' status from the user\'s task list that are pending completion.' },
  { tool: 'getPermissionRule', purpose: 'Fetches detailed information (full configuration) for a single hour-permission rule. Use when the user asks to show details, full settings, or everything about one rule  -  including when they refer to the rule only by its permission_name. Requires permission_id in the URL path: if the user did not supply a numeric id, call listPermissionRules first, resolve permission_id from permission_name, then call this tool.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=permission) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]).         3. Never show raw param_name keys, permission_id, or any internal IDs to the user  -  show names and labels only.         4. Resolve applicability via dependency tools - never expose raw IDs. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, listPermissionRules, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getPlanYearDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'getPlanYears', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch the plan year list including plan year name, start date, end date, and associated plans.' },
  { tool: 'getPlansForSpecificEnrollmentWindow', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch plans for a specific enrollment window.\n\ndependencyTools: getEnrollmentWindows' },
  { tool: 'getPlansForSpecificPlanYear', purpose: 'This action is used to fetch plans for a specific plan year.\n\ndependencyTools: getPlanYears' },
  { tool: 'getPresentByDefault', purpose: 'Fetches full detail of a single present-by-default group by record_id (path). Response includes name, from_date, to_date, reason, is_applicable_to_all, and applicable_for. Resolve record_id via listPresentByDefault. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).\n\ndependencyTools: listPresentByDefault, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getProjectDetails', purpose: 'Retrieve details for a specific project using projectId.' },
  { tool: 'getProjectUsers', purpose: 'This action is to get the users for a project. projectId can be taken from the tool getProjects  by setting the param assignedTo as all to get user of a specific project\n\ndependencyTools: getProjects' },
  { tool: 'getProjects', purpose: 'This action is to get projects. assignedTo is the user for whom the projects are assigned, default current user erecno will be used, assignedTo can be single user or multiple user with comma separated or all to get all users projects. projectStatus is either all or in-progress or completed default value is in-progress to get in-progress projects. clientId is id of clients with comma separated to get projects of selected clients. searchProjectName is used to search project with project name and searchProjectKey specify the type of search with any of the values all, equal, notEqual, startsWith, endsWith, contains, notContains and is send if searchProjectName key is sent. once the projects are fetched show them in table format with serial number. To add a project use addRecord tool with formLinkName P_TimesheetJobsList.' },
  { tool: 'getProviderDetail', purpose: 'This action is used to get detailed information of a specific benefit provider.\n\ndependencyTools: getProviders' },
  { tool: 'getProviders', purpose: 'This action is used to get the list of benefit providers or carriers configured in the organization including provider name, contact details, and associated plans.' },
  { tool: 'getRatingSummaryOfCycle', purpose: 'Fetches the employee count grouped by rating for a specific appraisal cycle. The cycleId in the URL must be obtained from the getAppraisalCycles tool response. The response includes the rating label, rating score, and the number of employees who received that rating in the cycle. Use when the user asks about rating distribution or rating summary of a cycle.\n\ndependencyTools: getAppraisalCycles' },
  { tool: 'getRecordByIDSectionWise', purpose: 'Retrieve a department form record using its Record ID in a section-wise format.' },
  { tool: 'getRecordCount', purpose: 'Fetches only the count of records from a Zoho People form. STRICT EMPLOYEE COUNT RULE: For any employee count, headcount, or users/employees tagged under a name/category/value, this is the ONLY data-fetch tool allowed. Do not use getEmployeeBasicDetails, getDepartmentDetails, or getRecords to discover, sample, or estimate employee counts. Use getFields on formLinkName employee to map the user\'s text to Employee form selectable fields such as Business Unit, Entity, Department, Sub Department, Location, Designation, Employee type, and similar employee attributes. For Picklist fields call getFieldOptions; for Lookup fields call getLookupOptions and match the user\'s text against option display values and IDs; do not call getFieldOptions for Lookup fields. Select the best matching field, option, and value only when the match is clear. If the intended field/form is unclear or multiple fields/options can match, ask the user which field display name they want to filter by before counting and show the best matching field/form display names as options. Do not choose a weak match, fetch a count, and present it as final. If the exact user text returns zero, do not broaden, shorten, split, or replace the user\'s value (for example, do not change a multi-word or compound value to only one keyword from it) unless the user explicitly asks to broaden the search. Instead ask whether to try a specific alternate matched option/field. Apply employee type/status filters only when the user explicitly requests them or a non-conflicting custom prompt supplies a default. searchParams must be a single pipe-delimited string of JSON filter objects using labelname values.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getFields, getFieldOptions, getLookupOptions' },
  { tool: 'getRecords', purpose: 'Fetches form records using formLinkName from identifyForm;      skip if form name is ambiguous. For system forms like employee, department, and location, the formLinkName is the same as employee or department or location as formLinkName.      To apply filters, call getFields with formLinkName, map field metadata to user intent from RECORD_FILTER, and pass constructed conditions as a searchParams string.      IMPORTANT: searchParams MUST ALWAYS be a single STRING. NEVER use a JSON array [{},{}] or a plain JSON object.      Ensure \'searchParams\' appears ONLY ONCE in the tool arguments.      If applying multiple filters, format them as multiple JSON objects separated by the pipe \'|\' character (e.g. "{filter1}|{filter2}").      Pass this as a single string value. When targeting the employee form, parse every zp[peopleuser:{id}]zp, treat extracted IDs as erecno, and pass them comma-separated in recordIds, passing the extracted IDs as recordIds=\'id1,id2\'.      Use the employeeDept parameter only when the user is clearly filtering based on department name.      Do not use the getFields tool if only department filtering is involved. This avoids redundant tool usage.      If the user wants to filter by multiple departments, pass them as a comma-separated string in the employeeDept value.      Use only the department names explicitly provided in the user prompt. Do not assume or add others.      Since the filter uses a contains match, if the users intent is to see all departments containing a specific keyword, collect and include all matching department names as the filter value.      CRITICAL FIELDS RULE (STRICT): The \'fields\' parameter MUST include ALL fields referenced in searchParams filters PLUS any additional fields needed for output.     Do NOT invoke getRecords unless every searchParams.searchField value is present in \'fields\'. Omitting filter fields from the \'fields\' parameter will cause \'Field name is invalid\' errors.     LABEL NAME RULE (STRICT): Both the \'fields\' entries AND the searchField value inside every searchParams filter object MUST be label names from getFields - NEVER user-facing display names. For example, use probation_end_date not Probation End Date, use Dateofjoining not Date of Joining. This applies to ALL employee form fields and ALL other form fields. Always call getFields first to get the correct label names before constructing fields or searchParams.      When the query involves total experience, the field stores values in MONTHS. You MUST convert the user\'s requested experience into months (e.g., 5 years = 60 months, 2 years = 24 months) and use the month value in searchText. NEVER pass year values directly.      For recency or time-based queries (e.g., recent, latest, newly, newest, recent joiners) where a precise time window cannot be determined confidently, set sortColumn to an appropriate date/time labelname returned by getFields (e.g., last modified, created time, joining date) and set sortBy=desc to return the most recent records;      do not guess date ranges.RECORD DISPLAY LIMIT (STRICT): Display at most 25 records in chat. If the result count exceeds 25, show the first 25 records, then ask the user if they want to view the full results via the records listing page (getRecordsViewUrl). Do NOT show more than 25 records in a single chat response. Do not include Zoho ID, Erecno, or ZUID in the assistant response content.     VIEW-PERMISSION FALLBACK (STRICT): If getRecords returns zero results, OR returns an error with code 7024 (message \'No records found\'), OR returns an error with code 7040 (message \'Permission denied to view record(s)\'), OR returns a \'Field name is invalid\' error for a field the user specified, the record may only be accessible in a non-default view type. GetFormRecordsAcrossViews is always available as a dependency - call it directly with the same formLinkName, fields, and searchParams. Do NOT retry getRecords. Do NOT fall back to getRecordsViewUrl and do NOT ask the user before completing this step.\nFallback:GetFormRecordsAcrossViews\nprecheckAction:getRecordCount\nprecheckCriteria:Must be fewer than 25 records\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getRecordCount, getFields, getRecordsViewUrl, GetFormRecordsAcrossViews' },
  { tool: 'getRecordsViewUrl', purpose: 'Fallback UI link to view form records when in-chat retrieval is impractical or showing all results is not feasible.      Use this tool when the user asks for the whole list of records, all records of a form, or a full list of records.      Usage rules: (1) Do NOT invoke directly. Always attempt identifyForm, then getFields, then getRecords first.      (2) RECORD LIMIT RULE (STRICT): getRecords MUST display at most 25 records in-chat. If the record count (from getRecordCount precheck or the tool response) exceeds 25, display the first 25 records in chat. Then inform the user that more records exist and ask if they would like to open the full records listing page. Invoke getRecordsViewUrl ONLY after the user confirms.      (3) If getRecords continues to fail after auto-correction retries, ask the user and invoke only on confirmation.      (4) Response format (strict): include a clickable markdown link in the assistant message using the redirectionHref value VERBATIM.      Use this exact pattern: [Open records page](URL). Do not mention internal key names or wrap the link in JSON. NEVER edit, append to, or extend the returned URL (no `?recordId=...`, no extra query params, no fragments, no template substitutions).      (5) Reuse the same searchParams you used for getRecords (build from RECORD_FILTER with labelname values).      (6) NEVER use a JSON array or object for searchParams; strictly pass it as a SINGLE STRING. Ensure \'searchParams\' appears ONLY ONCE in the tool arguments.      If multiple filters exist, join the JSON objects using the pipe \'|\' character (e.g. "{filter1}|{filter2}"). Never drop conditions.      (7) This action is ONLY a fallback tied to getRecords-do not use it for unrelated operations.      (8) Use the \'CONTAINS\' operator for comptype \'Lookup\' and \'Picklist\' in the record search URL.      (9) SCOPE (STRICT): This tool returns ONLY a records LISTING URL for the entire form (optionally filtered by searchParams). It does NOT return a per-single-record view URL, and no other tool does either. Never fabricate or assemble a single-record view URL (e.g., `/<form>/<form>_View?recordId=...`). After add/update/insert flows, do NOT produce \'View record\' / \'Open <form> Record\' links - confirm success in plain language and only offer to open the records listing page. See OUTPUT_HYGIENE_GUARD rule 6 for full enforcement.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getFields, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'getRegularizationSettings', purpose: 'Fetches regularization (attendance correction) configuration. Use when the user asks about how regularization is set up  -  whether it is enabled, max regularization days, whether reasons are mandatory, or configured reason list.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=regularization) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]).         3. Never show raw param_name keys, internal IDs, or record IDs to the user.         4. Resolve all referenced entities using dependency tools  -  never expose raw IDs.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams' },
  { tool: 'getRelatedChecklists', purpose: 'This action retrieves checklists associated with a specific record.its recordId must be provided as a parameter.' },
  { tool: 'getRelatedTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks associated with a specific record.its recordId must be provided as the parameter \'pkid\'.' },
  { tool: 'getRemotePolicies', purpose: 'Lists remote work policies (lightweight): policy_id, name, status, and applicability (resolve via getApplicableInfo; for user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo)) per policy. Use to enumerate policies or resolve policy_id by name before calling getRemotePolicy (full detail), updateRemotePolicy, or deleteRemotePolicy. When the user refers to a remote work policy by name or asks for details about a policy without providing its numeric id, call this tool first to resolve the policy_id. For detailed information about the rules, WFH reasons, applicability, and approval settings of one policy, call getRemotePolicy with the resolved policy_id.\n\ndependencyTools: getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getRemotePolicy', purpose: 'Fetches full detail for one remote work policy by policy_id (path segment): rules, WFH reasons, applicable_for, approval settings, etc. Call getRemotePolicies first to resolve policy_id.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=remotepolicy) first  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]).         3. Never show raw param_name keys, policy_id, or any internal IDs to the user  -  show names and labels only.         4. Resolve applicability via dependency tools - never expose raw IDs. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getRemotePolicies, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getReportSettings', purpose: 'Fetches attendance report access settings (Settings > Reports): whether managers can view reportee attendance reports, whether employees and managers can view or edit the Expected vs Worked Hours report, whether balance OT carry-over is enabled, and which payable/break detail columns managers can see on reportee attendance views.' },
  { tool: 'getReportees', purpose: 'This action fetches the reportees or subordinates of a specified employee.It requires the user\'s erecno (userId) or email.If the input is a name or any other value, use the getRecords tool to identify the correct user.Stop the process if more than one user matches the provided input.Use CURRENTUSER for the userId parameter when fetching the logged-in user\'s reportees/subordinates.Always set detailedResponseNeed as true and pass the user\'s erecno as userId.Set type as direct by default.Use type as all only when the user explicitly requests all reportees.In the response, the meaning of zoho_id depends on the context:For person entries (reportees and \'reporting_to\'), zoho_id represents the employee \'erecno\'(employee record number).For the designation object, zoho_id represents the designationId.Use the following URL for INVOKE_URL internally (do not show it to the user): \'/api/v3/__internal/employee/reportees/erecno\'. Do NOT display raw identifiers (erecno, zuid, zoho_id) in user-facing content; use employee name and emailId when needed.\n\ndependencyTools: getRecords, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getReviewStatus', purpose: 'Fetches the review completion status for a specific appraisal cycle. The cycleId in the URL must be obtained from the getAppraisalCycles tool response. Accepts an optional parameter review_type which filters by review type: \'self\' returns only self-review status, \'multirater\' returns only multi-rater/peer review status, \'appraiser\' returns only appraiser/manager review status. If review_type is not specified, the response includes the status of all configured review types (self, multirater, and appraiser) for that cycle. The response contains completion counts, pending counts, and overall progress for the requested review type(s).\n\ndependencyTools: getAppraisalCycles' },
  { tool: 'getRunningTimer', purpose: 'This action is to get currently running timer for the current user. It is used to list running timer for the user. if there is no result object in response then there is no running timer for the user.' },
  { tool: 'getShiftInfo', purpose: 'List all configured shifts for the organization with their metadata. Response is an array of shift objects with shiftId, shiftName, fTime, tTime, and colorCode. Use when the user asks about what shifts are configured or shift timings.' },
  { tool: 'getSkillView', purpose: 'Only for comparison and search by skills, level, experience, or manager use this mode , for fetching skills of specific user , use directly [getUserSkills]. Fetches a searchable view of employees and their skills with optional filters. Use when the user wants to search or browse employees by skills, level, experience, or manager. Parameters: skill_list (JSON array of skill IDs to filter by, up to 20), manager (manager employee record ID), level (skill level 0-10), from_exp (minimum years of experience 0-20), to_exp (maximum years of experience 0-20). Supports pagination via offset and limit. Dependencies: [getOrgSkills] to get skill IDs for the skill_list filter.\n\ndependencyTools: getOrgSkills' },
  { tool: 'getSpecificPolicies', purpose: 'Lists all specific attendance policies with essential details such as settings_id, name, and applicable_to (including type and ID). Ensures that all applicability IDs (e.g., department, shift, location) are resolved into their corresponding names using the appropriate dependency tool, rather than displaying raw IDs. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo). Use this to view available policies or to identify a policy\'s ID or name before performing actions like fetching details, updating, or deleting a specific policy.\n\ndependencyTools: getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, getShiftInfo' },
  { tool: 'getSpecificPolicyDetail', purpose: 'Fetches the full detail of a single specific attendance policy identified by settings_id (path segment). Response is nested by mode: policy, entry, officein_remotein, methods.         When presenting results:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams for each relevant mode block (mode=policy, mode=checkincheckout, mode=officeinremotein, mode=methods)  -  fetch labels and descriptions for each parameter in each block.         2. Show each setting as: [label]  -  [value] ([description]). Never show raw param_name keys or internal IDs.         3. Resolve applicability via dependency tools - show names, not raw IDs. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo).         Round-off vs Grace period (two completely separate features):         4. Round-off fields (early_check_in_round_off, late_check_in_round_off, early_check_out_round_off, late_check_out_round_off, and their *_mins variants)  -  adjusts the recorded punch time toward the shift boundary; it does NOT deduct leave. *_round_off=true snaps fully to the boundary; *_mins=N snaps only if within N minutes.         5. Grace period field (grace_period)  -  deducts leave when attendance violations exceed a configured frequency; it does NOT change the recorded punch time. Structured as {rules:[{Intime, Outtime, Worktime, Coretime, allowDays, graceMode, period, redStat, leavetype}]}. Dimensions applied are determined by which time fields are present: Intime (late check-in), Outtime (early check-out), Worktime (work-hours deficit), Coretime (core-hours violation). period is int enum: 0=weekly, 1=monthly, 2=pay-period. Never mix round-off with grace period  -  a late check-in tolerance goes inside a rule\'s Intime, not in late_check_in_mins.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         DISPLAY RULES (when summarising to the user):         - Working hours: Strict mode (is_min_hours_enabled=true, use_shift_hrs=false) -> show min_hours_full_day, max_hours_halfday, min_hours_half_day; hide hours_per_day.         - Working hours: Lenient mode (is_min_hours_enabled=false) -> show hours_per_day OR use_shift_hrs note; hide min_hours_full_day / max_hours_halfday / min_hours_half_day.         - Round-off: hide all *_round_off fields when is_round_off_avail=false. When grace_period has an Intime rule, hide late_check_in_round_off; when grace_period has an Outtime rule, hide early_check_out_round_off. round_off_hours always shows (when round-off enabled) and may co-exist with grace Worktime as a stricter inner tolerance.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getSpecificPolicies, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getShiftInfo, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'getStatus_or_getBreaks', purpose: 'This tool can be used by self user for either get user status or to get current day break details     To get user status          Retrieve allowedToCheckIn from the response. If it\'s true only then checkIn action can be allowed else return error  user is already in checked in state.          To get current day break details          Step-by-step Processing Instructions:        1. Go to: curDayBreakDetails.shiftBreakDets        2. For each breakId (which is the key inside shiftBreakDets), extract the following details:         breakId: the key itself         breakName: from the object\'s breakName field         payType:          If value is 0, interpret as Unpaid          If value is 1, interpret as Paid         breakTimeInSecs: convert to minutes using Math.floor(breakTimeInSecs / 60)        3. Format these into a user-friendly list with the structure:         breakName - Paid/Unpaid - duration in hh:mm format' },
  { tool: 'getStreamOptions', purpose: 'Lists the available streams so a stream and its streamId can be selected for stream-head operations. Send mode=\'deptStreamHead\'. Optionally pass searchKey to filter by stream name and use startIndex/limit (1-200) for pagination. Only When mode is chosen as \'deptStreamHead\' , optionally pass departmentId to filter stream options by department; resolve via getDepartmentDetails. Return the stream names to the user and retain each stream\'s id for use as $streamId$ in the DepartmentStreamHead tools.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails' },
  { tool: 'getSubKeyResults', purpose: 'Fetches sub key results under a specific parent key result. Requires keyResultId (long) and owner (employee erecno, long).' },
  { tool: 'getSurveyReport', purpose: 'Fetches the report for a specific survey including analytics such as employee count, response count, average score, and question-wise breakdown. Requires surveyId obtained from the mysurveyList tool. For recurring or repeat surveys, pass the optional recurrenceId parameter to fetch the report for a specific recurrence.\n\ndependencyTools: mysurveyList' },
  { tool: 'getTaskCount', purpose: 'This action retrieves the count of active tasks categorized by status as open (all tasks except completed), completed, and unassigned, along with the total task count based on filterBy all or my. By default, use filterBy=my as it returns the count of tasks where the user is the task owner. Using filterBy=all returns the count of all tasks, including those of your subordinates, based on permissions.In result, mention this open tasks count include all tasks that are not yet completed.' },
  { tool: 'getTasksByChecklistId', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks under the checklist associated with a specific record. It requires the unique identifiers \'pkid\' of the record and \'checklistid\' of the checklist.\n\ndependencyTools: getRelatedChecklists' },
  { tool: 'getTeamFinalRatingsOfCycle', purpose: 'Fetches the team final appraisal ratings of a specific cycle. The cycleId in the URL identifies the target cycle. The response includes cycle name, final rating score, rating label, and review completion details.\n\ndependencyTools: getAppraisalCycles' },
  { tool: 'getTeamMembersOnLeave', purpose: 'When a user asks about people on leave, determine whether the question is about their reportees or about a department. If the request is department-related and no department name is given, assume the current users department ID. If a department name is mentioned, first resolve it to a department ID using the `getDepartmentDetails` tool. If the user is only asking about their own reportees, you dont need a department ID just include incReporteeOnly as true. For dates, always ensure the range are valid date strings in the organization\'s date display format (use dateFormat from system instruction\'s DATE section). If no range is specified, use todays date. If a time frame is provided, format it the same way.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails' },
  { tool: 'getTeamObjectives', purpose: 'Fetches team objectives for a specific team member. Requires owner (employee erecno from getEmployeeBasicDetails), sIndx (start index), startPeriod and endPeriod (date range), okrStatus (status filter), and subMode (own|contribute|keyresults). Optional: approvalStatus (-1=Pending, 0=Rejected, 1=Approved, 2=All). Dependencies: [getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getEmployeeBasicDetails].\n\ndependencyTools: getOkrConfigData, getOkrStatusData, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getTimeLogDetails', purpose: 'Fetch details of a specific time log using the timelogId.' },
  { tool: 'getTimeLogs', purpose: 'Retrieve specific time logs from Zoho People for the provided user.' },
  { tool: 'getTimelogs', purpose: 'This action is to get timelogs for a user for a given period, user is the Employee for whom time logs are fetched default current user, fromDate will be start of period and toDate will be end of period (derive from today\'s date from system instruction\'s DATE section and convert to yyyy-MM-dd format), dateFormat default value is yyyy-MM-dd, default period is today, billingStatus is either billable or non-billable or all default value is all,approvalStatus is either approved or unapproved or all default value is all, jobId is used when the timelog of specific jobs needs to be fetched which gets from tool getJobs and sends with comma seperated if sending multiple id, projectId is used when the timelogs of specific projects needs to be fetched which gets from tool getProjects and are given with comma separated if haveing multiple id, clientId is used when the timelogs of specific clients needs to be fetched which gets from tool getClients and are given with comma separated if haveing multiple id. list param is false by default\n\ndependencyTools: getJobs, getProjects, getClients' },
  { tool: 'getTimerComments', purpose: 'Retrieve comments added to the specified time log.' },
  { tool: 'getTimesheetDetails', purpose: 'Retrieve details of a specific timesheet by passing the timesheet ID as a query parameter.' },
  { tool: 'getTimesheets', purpose: 'Fetch timesheets for a specific user from Zoho People.' },
  { tool: 'getTopProjectJobs', purpose: 'This action is to get top or most worked or active jobs for a project. The logged hours of these jobs are high in this project. projectId can be taken from the tool getProjects by setting the param assignedTo as all and searchProjectName with name and searchProjectKey with contains. The result will have a totalHours key which is in minutes and should convert them to hours before displaying.\n\ndependencyTools: getProjects' },
  { tool: 'getTopProjectUsers', purpose: 'This action is to get top or best performing users for a project. projectId can be taken from the tool getProjects  by setting the param assignedTo as all and searchProjectName with name and searchProjectKey with contains. The result contains totalHours key in minutes, convert them to hours and display.\n\ndependencyTools: getProjects' },
  { tool: 'getTrackTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks created by the current user. By default, it returns tasks with \'Open\' status and \'Moderate\' priority unless otherwise specified. Retrieval starts from the specified record index (stIndex), which begins at 1. Additionally, the action provides a count of tasks created by the user, categorized by status.       New task records can be created using the \'addRecord\' API. The Start Date and Due Date default to the current date, while the status defaults to \'Open\' and the priority to \'Moderate\'. The task owner defaults to the current user unless otherwise specified' },
  { tool: 'getUnassignedGoalUsersReport', purpose: 'Fetches the Unassigned Goal Users report under Performance Appraisal Reports. Lists employees who have no goals assigned within a given period for a manager\'s team (or for the whole organisation when used by an admin). Parameter usage: managerId is the erecno of the manager whose team is being viewed, and the response represents that team\'s data. from and to define the period in Organisation date format strictly follow the date format or else ask the user and default to the first and last day of the current month when the user does not specify a range. sIndex is 1-based and returns up to 100 records per page (next page is 101, then 201, and so on). employeeStatus must always be sent as [19] (active employees only). repType must be \'adminReports\' as default value , otherwise \'teamReports\' (manager fetching their team\'s data). Set recordcount=true when the user only wants a count of unassigned-goal users; otherwise omit it or set false. dateType is a JSON array describing which date the from/to range applies to: 0=Created Date, 1=Start Date, 2=Completed Date, 3=Due Date; defaults to an empty array when the user does not specify. The locationArr/departmentArr/entityArr/businessUnitArr/divisionArr/designationArr filters are not used by this tool. Show the user suggestion that this is 100 records fetched , ask user for next fetch until last fetch is less than 100 records' },
  { tool: 'getUnassignedSkillEmployeesReport', purpose: 'Fetches the Unassigned Skill Employees report under Performance Appraisal Skill Set Reports. Lists employees who have no skills assigned. Parameter usage: repType must be \'adminReports\' as default value , otherwise \'teamReports\' (manager fetching their team\'s data). sIndex is 1-based and returns up to 20 records per page (next page is 101, then 201, and so on). Set recordCount=true when the user only wants a count of unassigned-skill employees; otherwise omit it or set false. employeeArr is an optional JSON array of employee erecnos to restrict the report to specific employees; leave empty to include all applicable employees in the selected scope. Show the user suggestion that this is 100 records fetched , ask user for next fetch until last fetch is less than 100 records' },
  { tool: 'getUnits', purpose: 'Retrieves a list of all business units in the organization structure. Supports pagination via \'offset\' (1-based page number, default 1) and \'limit\' (records per page, 1-200, default 200). Use the \'is_tagged\' parameter to filter: 1 = units tagged under a legal entity in the hierarchy, 0 = units not tagged. Only active, non-dummy records are returned. IMPORTANT: If the user refers to Business Units using a custom display name (as specified in the system prompt), use this tool - do NOT use any other tool such as getAllFiles or getRecords.' },
  { tool: 'getUntaggedUserCompetencies', purpose: 'Fetches competencies from the org library that are not yet tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUntaggedUserKras', purpose: 'Fetches KRAs from the org library that are not yet tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUntaggedUserSkills', purpose: 'Fetches skills from the org library that are not yet tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserAvailability', purpose: 'This tool fetches the availability status of one or more specific users.                       It does not support fetching data for all users at once.                      Either erecno or empid must be provided to identify the user(s) for whom data is required.                      Both parameters support single or multiple values.                       Multiple users can be specified by providing their identifiers as a comma-separated string.                                            Response parsing:                          Path: result[i]                              erecno - Employee record number (string)                              isUserAvailable - Boolean value indicating user availability (true/false)                              isOfficeIn - Boolean value indicating whether the user is currently in office (true/false)                              isUserOnBreak - Boolean value indicating whether the user is currently on break (true/false)                      Format these into a user-friendly list with the structure:                           * If the user is available and in office -> \'Available (In Office)\'                             * If the user is available but isOfficeIn is false -> \'Available (Remote)\'                             * If the user is on break -> \'Not Available (On Break)\'                             * If the user is not available -> \'Not Available\'                                            Employee Name - [Availability Status] Example: EmployeeName - Available (In Office), Not Availabile (On Break), Availabile (Remote)' },
  { tool: 'getUserCompetencies', purpose: 'Fetches the competencies tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserEnrollmentBeneficiaries', purpose: 'Fetches the list of all beneficiaries for an employee\'s enrollment.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks about their own enrollment beneficiaries, use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s enrollment beneficiaries, resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserEnrollmentDetail', purpose: 'Fetches detailed information of a specific user enrollment including plan details, coverage selection, dependents covered, contribution breakdown, and enrollment dates.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks about their own enrollment details, use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s enrollment details, resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.      Requires an enrollment ID which can be obtained from getEmployeeBenefitPlans response.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserEnrollmentWindowPlans', purpose: 'Fetches the benefit plans an employee is eligible to enroll in within a specific enrollment window. Unlike getEmployeeBenefitPlans (which returns already-enrolled plans), this returns the available/selectable plans the employee can choose during that window.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks \'show plans I can enroll in\', \'what benefits are available for open enrollment\', use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s enrollment options, use the target employee\'s erecno from getEmployeeBasicDetails.      Requires the enrollment window ID, which must first be obtained by calling getUserEnrollmentWindows. Returns eligible plan details: plan name, provider, coverage tiers, premium/cost options, employer contribution, and eligibility criteria. These results feed into submitEnrollments or singlePlanEnrollment to complete the enrollment.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollmentWindows, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserEnrollmentWindows', purpose: 'Fetches the list of benefit enrollment windows currently open or available to an employee - including Open Enrollment, New Hire Enrollment, and Qualifying Life Event (QLE) windows triggered by events like marriage, birth of a child, or change in employment status. An enrollment window is a time-bound period during which the employee can enroll in, change, or waive benefit plans.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks \'can I enroll in benefits now\', \'show my open enrollment windows\', \'is there an enrollment period active for me\', use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s enrollment windows (\'show John\'s enrollment windows\', \'can employee X enroll\'), first resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails, then use that erecno. Admins can view any employee\'s enrollment windows.      Returns each window\'s ID, type (Open / New Hire / QLE), start and end dates, and current status (open/closed/upcoming). This is the entry point to the enrollment flow and is required before calling getUserEnrollmentWindowPlans or submitEnrollments.      STRICT (RESPONSE INTERPRETATION): If the response returns an empty enrollment_windows array, this means the employee currently has NO open enrollment windows (which is normal outside of enrollment periods). Inform the user that no active enrollment windows exist - do NOT claim any configuration, permission, or IAM issue. An empty array is a valid business response, not a system error.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserEnrollments', purpose: 'Admin-scoped action (requires dataadmin permission) that returns the list of user enrollments for a specific benefit plan - including enrollment status, plan details, coverage, and effective dates. Use as the listing source before chaining into per-enrollment admin actions like approveEnrollment, denyEnrollment, terminateEnrollment, getEnrollmentDetail, getAdminEnrollmentBeneficiaries, or addAdminBeneficiary.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'getUserGoals', purpose: 'Fetches the goals assigned to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Supports pagination via offset and limit. By default set limit as 5. Filtering parameters: status filters by goal completion status (1 = All Goals, 2 = In Progress, 3 = Completed, 4 = Overdue, 5 = Delayed,0=In Progress and InComplete ,6=Approved Goals , 7=UnApproved Goals , 8=Archived Goals). period_status filters by goal time period (1 = All Goals, 2 = This Week, 3 = Last Week, 4 = This Month, 5 = Last Month). from_date and to_date filter goals within a custom date range. date_types filters by goal date category (1-4, comma-separated). Use status when the user asks about goals by completion state (e.g. overdue goals, completed goals). Use period_status when the user asks about goals by time period (e.g. this week\'s goals, last month\'s goals). Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. In the response, approval_status has the following meanings: -2 refers to No Approval, -1 refers to Pending, 1 refers to Approved, 0 refers to Rejected. For fetching archived goals , status should be 8\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserKras', purpose: 'Fetches the KRAs tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. In the response, approval_status has the following meanings: -2 refers to No Approval, -1 refers to Pending, 1 refers to Approved, 0 refers to Rejected. Hide the type in the response. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserPlanCoverages', purpose: 'Calculates and fetches coverage and premium details for an employee\'s benefit plan.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks about their own plan coverages, use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s plan coverages, resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserPlanDetail', purpose: 'Fetches plan details including attachments for a specific employee\'s enrolled plan.      SELF USAGE: When the user asks about their own plan details, use the current user\'s erecno.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: When the user asks about another employee\'s plan details, resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserPlanYears', purpose: 'Fetches the list of benefit plan years (e.g., 2023, 2024, 2025) available to an employee. A plan year represents the yearly coverage cycle under which the employee\'s benefit plans (medical, dental, vision, etc.) are grouped.      SELF vs OTHER EMPLOYEE: If the user asks about their own plan years (\'show my benefit plan years\', \'my coverage years\'), use the current user\'s erecno. If the user asks about another employee\'s plan years (\'show John\'s plan years\', \'what plan years does employee X have\'), first resolve the employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails, then use that erecno.      ADMIN USAGE: Admins can use this tool to view any employee\'s plan years by providing the target employee\'s erecno. Non-admins can view their own plan years.      STRICT (PREREQUISITE TOOL): This action is the MANDATORY first step before getEmployeeBenefitPlans. The plan_year_id returned here MUST be passed into getEmployeeBenefitPlans via filterData.plan_years - without it the downstream endpoint returns an empty plans array. If the user asks \'show my plans\', \'show my benefits\' or any coverage query, call this tool FIRST silently to obtain the active plan year (the entry with is_current=true), then chain getEmployeeBenefitPlans.      Returns plan year IDs, labels, start/end dates, and active/current-year flags. Optional filterData can be passed to narrow results.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUserSkills', purpose: 'Fetches the skills tagged to a specific employee. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails]. By default set limit as 5.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'getUsersBySkills', purpose: 'This action retrieves a list of users based on one or more specified skills. The skills parameter is required and must be provided as a comma-separated list of skill names (up to 10). The limit parameter acts as a start index for pagination, indicating the position from which results should begin. The levels parameter is optional and supports filtering by skill proficiency level and it accepts a comma-separated list of up to 5 values, each constrained to 0 to 10.  The maximum permissible level depends on the configured maxSkillLevel, which can be obtained from the getUserSkills action response.' },
  { tool: 'getWFHApprovals', purpose: 'This tool fetches Work From Home (WFH) / Remote Work / WFH Exception approval records. It internally uses the getApprovals tool.      When invoking getApprovals, always pass: serviceName=\'Attendance\' and formName=\'P_ATT_WFH_REQUEST\'.      Use action=\'myApprovals\' to get WFH/Remote Work/WFH Exception requests pending your approval, or action=\'myRequests\' to get WFH/Remote Work/WFH Exception requests you have submitted.      Default to action=\'myApprovals\' with approvalStatus=\'pending\' if the user does not specify.\n\ndependencyTools: getApprovals' },
  { tool: 'getWFHPolicyInfo', purpose: 'This tool fetches the Work From Home (WFH) / Remote Work / WFH Exception policy configuration and available balance for the current user or a specified employee. The response contains:      - allowedDays: total WFH days allowed per period      - availableDays: remaining WFH/Remote Work days the user can still apply for      - period: the period type for the WFH allowance      - isDescriptionMandatory: whether a description/reason text is required when applying      - isAttachementMandatory: whether a file attachment is required when applying      - isWfhReasonsEnabled: whether predefined WFH reasons are configured      - wfhReasons: array of configured WFH reason strings (only present if isWfhReasonsEnabled is true)      - restrictedWeekdays: weekdays on which WFH/Remote Work is not allowed      - isWfhApprConfigured: whether WFH approval workflow is configured      - recentRequestDate: the date of the most recently raised WFH/Remote Work request by the user      Use this tool before creating a WFH/Remote Work/WFH Exception request to check available balance, mandatory fields, valid reasons, and the date of the recently raised request.' },
  { tool: 'getWatchListTasks', purpose: 'This action retrieves tasks from the user\'s watchlist where the user is tagged in task comments. By default, it uses status alltasks (0) and priority alltasks (0) if not specified.' },
  { tool: 'getWeightedAverageOfEmployee', purpose: 'Fetches the weighted average rating for a specific employee. The employee_erecno in the URL must be obtained from the getEmployeeBasicDetails tool response. The response includes the overall weighted average score computed across last five cycles of the employee. Use when the user asks about the overall or weighted average rating of a employee\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'identifyForm', purpose: 'This tool returns the custom forms list available in Zoho People' },
  { tool: 'leavePreview', purpose: 'Dependency-only tool for the applyLeave flow. Load and call it when the user wants to apply leave - not as a standalone balance tool.      Previews balance impact of the proposed leave (current balance, currentBooking, balanceAfterBooking, yearEndBalance, lop) before submit.      When showing the preview in the applyLeave flow, always include current balance, balance after booking, and year end balance.      Call after getLeaveBalance has resolved the leave type name to id. Pass employee, leavetype, from, to, and dayDetails ({} for default full days; per-date count/session/startTime/endTime when partial/hour leave is needed).      For booked vs balance or general balance questions, use bookedAndBalance instead.' },
  { tool: 'listAbsentSchedulers', purpose: 'Lists all configured Absent Scheduler rules (Settings > Automation > Absent Scheduler). Each scheduler runs daily, marks no-swipe employees absent for a specific attendance calendar date, optionally pushes to Leave, and sends emails. TIME is packed (see createAbsentScheduler). Each entry includes record_id, name, time, push_absent_to_leave, notify_through_mail, and applicability.' },
  { tool: 'listAllCategory', purpose: 'Fetch all HR helpdesk case categories available to the current user. Use this tool when the user asks \'what categories are available\', \'show me case categories\', \'list case categories\', \'list all categories\', or when adding a new case and the category is not yet known. Mode values: \'userListing\' (default, for employees), \'agentListing\' (for agents viewing their assigned categories), \'adminListing\' (for HR admins managing categories). Always send mode=\'userListing\' unless the user is a confirmed agent or admin.' },
  { tool: 'listBreaks', purpose: 'Lists all configured break definitions (Settings > Break). Optional filters: break_mode (true=auto-deduct, false=manual), pay_type (0=unpaid, 1=paid), shift_ids (JSONArray). Supports pagination via scroll_index and optional sorting. applicable_shifts are shift IDs - call getShiftInfo to show shift names.\n\ndependencyTools: getShiftInfo' },
  { tool: 'listCaseSubCategories', purpose: 'Fetch all subcategories available under a specific HR helpdesk category. Use this tool when the user wants to see subcategories for a category, or when you need to show subcategory options before changing the subcategory of a case. Always send categoryId (required). Trigger phrases: \'list subcategories\', \'show subcategories\', \'what subcategories are available\', \'subcategory options\'.\n\ndependencyTools: listAllCategory' },
  { tool: 'listHolidayGallery', purpose: 'Use when leave-type/holiday gallery view is needed, or when the user wants to add a holiday but has not mentioned a holiday date/name yet - fetch and show the country holiday gallery so they can pick from standard holidays. Always pass method=gallery_list, country (default in if unspecified), and year (default current calendar year). Present the returned holidays (name + date) as a selectable gallery list. Do not use for listing already-configured org holidays (listholidays). Do not invent holiday dates.' },
  { tool: 'listMyCases', purpose: 'Use this tool ONLY when an HR agent or support agent asks for cases ASSIGNED TO THEM for handling or resolving. This filters by ASSIGNEDTO field. Valid trigger phrases: \'cases assigned to me\', \'my assigned cases\', \'cases in my queue\', \'cases I need to handle\', \'cases I am handling\'. DO NOT USE this tool when the user says \'I raised\', \'I submitted\', \'I created\', \'my requests\', \'requests I raised\', \'cases I opened\' - use listMyRequests for those instead. Always send method=\'myHrCases\' and myCasesJson with index=1 and status=1 (Open) by default. Status values: 1=Open, 2=In Progress, 3=Pending, 4=On Hold, 5=Closed, 6=Cancelled. Response fields: use \'caseId\' as the case identifier, \'subject\' for the title, \'statusLabel\' for status display.' },
  { tool: 'listMyRequests', purpose: 'This is the PRIMARY tool for any user (employee/requestor) asking to view cases they RAISED, SUBMITTED, or CREATED. Valid trigger phrases: \'my cases\', \'my tickets\', \'my helpdesk cases\', \'cases I raised\', \'requests I raised\', \'cases I submitted\', \'cases I created\', \'cases I opened\', \'my pending requests\', \'my helpdesk requests\'. Always send method=\'myHrCasesRequest\' and myCaseRequestJson with status=\'\' (empty string for all statuses) and index=1 by default. Increment index for pagination. Response fields: use \'caseId\' as the case identifier, \'subject\' for the title, \'statusLabel\' for status display.' },
  { tool: 'listOnboardingRecords', purpose: 'Fetches the list of onboarding candidates or employees. REQUIRED PARAMS: reportType (String) - "P_Candidate" for candidates, "P_Employee" for employees; isnewui (boolean) - always pass true; searchJson (JSONObject) - always required, pass {} for no filters. CANDIDATE ONBOARDING_STATUS values (only for reportType=P_Candidate): 0=Not Triggered, 1=Triggered (yet to accept invite), 2=In Progress, 3=Completed by Admin, 4=Completed by Candidate, 5=Reopened, 6=Converted to Employee, -7=Inactive. EMPLOYEE ONBOARDING_STATUS values (only for reportType=P_Employee): 2=In Progress, 3=Completed. Employees do not have Triggered, Reopened, Converted to Employee, or Inactive states. SEARCHJSON FILTERS: ONBOARDING_STATUS (String, comma-separated ints) - use candidate values for P_Candidate, employee values for P_Employee; omit key to return all supported statuses. CANDIDATE_NAME or EMPLOYEE_NAME (String) - name contains-match; not an email search. DEPARTMENTNAME (longarray) - department IDs; resolve name to ID via getDepartmentDetails first. LOCATION (longarray) - location IDs; resolve name to ID via getLocationDetails first. DESIGNATIONNAME or ROLENAME (longarray) - designation or role IDs. DATEOFJOINING (String) - filter by date of joining. CANDIDATEEMAIL (String, candidates only) - exact email match; use when the user provides an email address. CID (String, candidates only) - MUST pass only the numeric suffix of the candidate display ID. NORMALIZATION RULE: when the user provides a candidate display ID in any format - e.g. CND-35, CND35, cnd 35 - strip the alphabetic prefix and any hyphen/space separator, then pass ONLY the digits as CID (e.g. pass \'35\' for both CND-35 and CND35). Do NOT pass the full display ID (CND-35, CND35, etc.) as CID - it will not match. The top-level \'prefix\' field in the response holds the display prefix; prepend it to filterData.CID when showing the ID to the user. CANDIDATEID (longarray, candidates only) - filter by PKID directly. EMPLOYEEMAILALIAS (String, employees only) - exact email match for employees. EMPLOYEEID (String, employees only) - the human-readable employee ID (e.g. \'EMP-001\'); pass the exact value including any prefix. ERECNO (longarray, employees only) - filter by employee erecno/PKID directly. OPTIONAL PARAMS: start (int) - pagination offset, default 0. CANDIDATE UI VIEW MAPPINGS: Not Triggered: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="0". Triggered: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="1". In Progress: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="1,2,4,5". Onboarded: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="3". Converted to Employee: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="6" then display only filterData rows where ONBOARDING_STATUS=6. All: pass empty searchJson {}. EMPLOYEE UI VIEW MAPPINGS: In Progress: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="2". Completed: pass ONBOARDING_STATUS="3". All: pass empty searchJson {}. RESPONSE: always read and display records from filterData (array of individual records). Do NOT use reportcount - it is a summary count and does not reflect the applied filter. Each filterData record contains: PKID (always use this for all operation params - deletegroup, candidate_ids, record_id, recordId, erecnoobj, etc.), EMAILALIAS (the candidate\'s or employee\'s email). Candidate records also contain: CID (numeric part of display ID - prepend the top-level \'prefix\' when showing to user). The top-level candidateFormId must be passed as formId in triggerCandidateOnboarding. DISPLAY RULE: When showing onboarding status to the user, MUST use only text labels - MUST NOT show raw ONBOARDING_STATUS numbers. Candidate labels: Not Triggered, Triggered, In Progress, Completed by Admin, Completed by Candidate, Reopened, Converted to Employee, Inactive. Employee labels: In Progress, Completed. Never fabricate IDs.\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'listPermissionRules', purpose: 'Lists hour-permission rules (short-leave) with lightweight summary fields only: permission_id, permission_name, status, is_applicable_to_all; applicable_fields when scoped. Does NOT return full rule configuration  -  for detailed information use getPermissionRule. For user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo). When the user gives a rule label or name (any text such as a custom permission_name) or asks for detailed info by name, call this first and match permission_name (fuzzy match ok) to obtain permission_id. Same permission_name key as getPermissionRule and create/update/deletePermissionRule. Org-wide hour-permission module toggle is on PUT /settings/methods (is_permission_enabled).\n\ndependencyTools: getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'listPresentByDefault', purpose: 'Lists all configured Present by Default groups (Settings > Automation > Present by Default). Applicable employees are auto-marked Present at midnight (shift timezone) without check-in/out; absent scheduler does not apply; approved leave overrides. Each entry includes record_id, name, from_date, to_date, reason, and applicability.' },
  { tool: 'listholidays', purpose: 'This tool fetches holidays applicable to the current user, where from and to are derived from user intent: use specified date ranges or relative periods if provided; for all holidays, set from to year start and to to year end and return past and upcoming sections; for past holidays, set from to year start and to to today (system DATE); for planning or general queries, default to upcoming holidays with from as today (system DATE) and to as year end.If past and upcoming holidays are asked together provide in separate sections.' },
  { tool: 'lms_course_batches', purpose: 'List batches for a specific Blended Learning course in the LMS. Ensure the `courseId` is sourced by using the `lms_courses` tool to search with the course name. If multiple courses are found, prompt the user to select the desired course.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_courses' },
  { tool: 'lms_course_progress_report', purpose: 'Retrieve a detailed progress report for a specific course, including completion statistics and progress details.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_courses' },
  { tool: 'lms_courses', purpose: 'Search for LMS courses for a user. First, search in the catalog; if not found, search in \'my courses\'; finally, search in the organization. Respond with the course URL formatted as a hyperlink: [courseName](courseUrl). For joined courses related query use the `lms_learner_progress_report` tool.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_learner_progress_report' },
  { tool: 'lms_enroll_course', purpose: 'Enroll users into an LMS course. If the API returns \'this course is not applicable,\' prompt for confirmation to proceed with forced enrollment using `modeOfadd=\'applicablemember\'`. On success, provide a concise message with enrolled users and course name as a hyperlink [courseName](courseUrl). Use `lms_courses` to obtain the course URL.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_courses' },
  { tool: 'lms_learner_progress_report', purpose: 'Fetches a comprehensive report of a learner\'s course progress. Note: maximum range is one year.' },
  { tool: 'lms_learning_plan_course_progress_report', purpose: 'Fetches progress details for all courses within a user\'s learning plan' },
  { tool: 'lms_learning_plan_progress_report', purpose: 'Provides a summary of a user\'s learning plan progress, including completion status and progress metrics.' },
  { tool: 'lms_learning_plans', purpose: 'Search or Lists learning plans available. First, search in the catalog; if not found, search in \'my\' plan; finally, search in the organization.' },
  { tool: 'lms_send_mandatory_reminder_spl', purpose: 'Sends reminders to users for mandatory items they have not yet completed for self paced learning courses. The courseId parameter is required and must be obtained using the `lms_courses` tool by searching for the course name.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_courses' },
  { tool: 'lms_send_overdue_notification', purpose: 'Send overdue notifications to users for incomplete items in self-paced learning courses. Obtain the `courseId` by searching for the course name using the `lms_courses` tool and specify the `learnerId` (erecno). If a failure response is received, prompt the user to ensure that notifications are enabled.\n\ndependencyTools: lms_courses, getEmployeeBasicDetails, getRecords' },
  { tool: 'mapGoalsToKra', purpose: 'Maps goals to a given KRA for a specific employee. The goal_ids parameter (JSON array of goal IDs) and kra parameter (KRA ID) are required. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment.                      while calling getUserGoals tools ,strictly set hide_kra as true . Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras, getUserGoals] .In the response of getUserKras, approval_status has the following meanings: -2 refers to No Approval, -1 refers to Pending, 1 refers to Approved, 0 refers to Rejected. Restrict the users [-1 , 0] approval_status not to be mapped\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserKras, getUserGoals' },
  { tool: 'mySurveyStatusCount', purpose: 'Fetches the current user\'s survey status counts. Returns mysurvey_status_count object with keys: all (total surveys), expired (expired surveys), completed (completed surveys), actionpending (surveys pending user action). Use this when the user asks how many surveys they have pending, completed, or expired.' },
  { tool: 'mycompensation', purpose: 'This action is used to get logged in user\'s compensation details which includes salary, revision histories, breakup components i.e salary and benefit components.' },
  { tool: 'mysurveyList', purpose: 'Fetches the list of surveys assigned to the current user. Supports optional filtering via a filter JSON parameter with keys: survey_name (search by name), status (0=All, 1=Action Pending, 2=Completed, 3=Expired), and survey_type (1=enps, 2=engagement, 4=pulse). Returns survey details including survey_id, survey_name, type, status, cover_image, respondent_identity, and created_by_details. For surveys with status Action Pending, construct the attempt URL using the format: /<portalName>/survey/<url> where <portalName> is obtained from the system context (organizationPortalName) and <url> is the url field from each survey in the response. Present this as a clickable markdown link so the user can take or attempt the survey directly.' },
  { tool: 'pickUnassignedTask', purpose: 'This action picks unassigned tasks, which are tasks assigned to specific groups, roles, departments, or locations. A user eligible to pick a task must be either an admin or a member of the assigned group. The action requires the task ID to assign the user as the task owner. The task ID can be retrieved by using the getMyTasks API with the filter set to \'all\', status set to \'unassigned\' (-1), and optionally filtering by task name.\n\ndependencyTools: getMyTasks' },
  { tool: 'publishBenefitPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to publish a benefit plan making it available to employees.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'publishJobSchedule', purpose: 'This action is to publish the job schedules for the given period for the given users. fromDate is start of period and todate is end of period, user is erecno of user for whom the job schedules need to be published and will be send as comma separated values' },
  { tool: 'reTriggerOnboarding', purpose: 'Re-triggers the onboarding process for a candidate or employee, resetting their progress back to In Progress. HARD CONSTRAINT: MUST NOT be used for candidates in Not Triggered or Converted to Employee state - if the candidate\'s status is Not Triggered or Converted to Employee, MUST NOT proceed and MUST tell the user that re-trigger is not supported for that status. Works for candidates in In Progress, Completed by Admin, Completed by Candidate, or Reopened state. Works for employees in In Progress or Completed state. Call listOnboardingRecords first to find the PKID and verify the current status is a valid re-trigger state. Body params: record_id (long, PKID from listOnboardingRecords), ob_type (\'candidate\' or \'employee\'). When informing the user about status, use text labels - do not show status numbers. Requires confirmation before executing since this resets onboarding progress.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'reopenOnboarding', purpose: 'Reopens the onboarding process for a candidate. HARD CONSTRAINT: MUST ONLY work for candidates whose current status is Completed by Candidate. If the candidate\'s status is anything other than Completed by Candidate - including Completed by Admin, In Progress, Reopened, or any other value - MUST NOT proceed and MUST tell the user that reopen is not supported for that status. Use the text status label when informing the user - do not show status numbers. Does not work for employees at all. Call listOnboardingRecords first to find and confirm the candidate PKID and verify status is Completed by Candidate (ONBOARDING_STATUS=4 in the response) before invoking. Pass the PKID as candidate_id (long) in the request body. Optionally accepts a message to send to the candidate via the mail_json parameter. Requires confirmation before executing.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'reopenTask', purpose: 'This action changes the status of the task to \'Open\',it requires taskid.\n\ndependencyTools: getMyTasks' },
  { tool: 'replyCaseComment', purpose: 'Use this tool to post a reply or comment on an HR helpdesk case. Trigger phrases: \'reply to case\', \'add comment\', \'respond to case\', \'post reply\', \'comment on case\', \'send reply to helpdesk case\', \'leave a message on case\'. TWO scenarios: (A) If the user already provided a caseId - call this tool directly with caseId and comment. (B) If no caseId is provided - use dependency tools to show the user\'s cases, ask them to pick one, then call this tool with the chosen caseId.\n\ndependencyTools: viewCase, listMyCases, listMyRequests' },
  { tool: 'requestedVsEscalatedCases', purpose: 'Retrieve a report of requested and escalated cases. In the payload, set method=\'slaEsclationReport\' and repType=\'adminReports\' Here duration can have 5 values 1,2,3,4,5. 1 is for last 24 hours, 2 is for last 48 hours, 3 is past week, 4 is for last month and 5 is for last 3 months. If duration is not mentioned then it will be considered as 3..' },
  { tool: 'resendInvitation', purpose: 'Resends the onboarding invitation to an existing candidate. HARD CONSTRAINT: MUST ONLY work for candidates in Triggered state. If the candidate\'s current status is anything other than Triggered, MUST NOT proceed and MUST tell the user that resend invitation is only available for candidates in Triggered state. Do not show status numbers to the user - use the text label Triggered. Call listOnboardingRecords first to find the candidate and verify their status is Triggered (ONBOARDING_STATUS=1 in the response). Pass the PKID as a single-element JSONArray in candidate_ids. Do NOT use CID - it is an internal sequence number and will cause a conflict error. Never fabricate the candidate ID.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'runPresentByDefaultForPast', purpose: 'Runs a present-by-default group retroactively for a past date range (from_date to to_date). Modifies historical attendance records - confirm with the user before running. Resolve record_id via listPresentByDefault.\n\ndependencyTools: listPresentByDefault' },
  { tool: 'startTimer', purpose: 'This action is to add or start or resume or pause timer for self or current user, jobName is a job that time is logged, user is the Employee for whom timer is added, workDate is the date to log time (derive from today\'s date from system instruction\'s DATE section and convert to yyyy-MM-dd format), hours is duration for the timelog, billingStatus is either billable or non-billable default value is billable, timer value is start to start or resume timer and stop to stop the running timer, timeLogId is id of timelog to specify the pause or resume or stop the timer that can be from fetched from tools getRunningTimer or running timer for getTimelogs tool\n\ndependencyTools: getRunningTimer, getTimelogs' },
  { tool: 'submitEnrollments', purpose: 'Enrolls an employee in a list of plans from an enrollment window.      SELF USAGE: Use the current user\'s erecno when enrolling in their own plans.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: Resolve the target employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollmentWindowPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'sumbitTimesheet', purpose: 'This action is to create or submit timesheet or submit timelogs or save timesheet as draft or save timelogs as a draft for a user for a given period. timesheetName is concat of  text Timesheet and small bracket open and fromDate and hifun key and toDate and small bracket close with spaces, fromDate will be start of period and toDate will be end of period needs to be sent in yyyy-MM-dd date format, dateFormat value is yyyy-MM-dd, billableStatus is all by default, user is the Employee for whom timesheeet to be created by default current user, sendforApproval is by default true and if user want to submit timesheet as draft then its needs to be sent as false.     jobId is used when the timelog of specific jobs needs to be submitted which gets from tool getJobs and sends with comma seperated if sending multiple id, projectId is used when the timelogs of specific projects needs to be submitted which gets from tool getProjects and are given with comma separated if haveing multiple id, clientId is used when the timelogs of specific clients needs to be submitted which gets from tool getClients and are given with comma separated if haveing multiple id\n\ndependencyTools: getJobs, getProjects, getClients' },
  { tool: 'surveyList', purpose: 'Fetches the list of surveys created by the current user. Requires mode parameter: enps (eNPS surveys), engagement (engagement surveys), pulse (pulse surveys). Also requires startIndex and limit for pagination. Returns survey details including survey_id, survey_name, employee_count, response_count, response_percentage, opening_time, closing_time, current_state, and status. Supports optional filter JSON with keys: survey_name, status, start_date (yyyyMMdd), end_date (yyyyMMdd). Use mysurveyList instead to fetch surveys assigned to the current user for responding.' },
  { tool: 'tagUserCompetencies', purpose: 'Tags existing org-level competencies to a specific employee. The competencies parameter is required and must be a JSON array of competency objects following the addcompetencyuser template in which competency param for competency record id , weightage param for weightage alone should be allowed. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserCompetencies]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserCompetencies' },
  { tool: 'tagUserKras', purpose: 'Tags existing org-level KRAs to a specific employee. The kras parameter is required and must be a JSON array of KRA objects following the add template in which kra param for kra id, weightage param for weightage alone should be allowed. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserKras]. If users specifies the kra not in the untagged kra list and then forward to action create and tag kra [addAndTagUserKra]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserKras' },
  { tool: 'tagUserSkills', purpose: 'Tags existing org-level skills to a specific employee. The skills parameter is required and must be a JSON array of skill objects following the addskilluser template in which skill param for skill id, level param for skill level alone should be allowed. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserSkills]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUntaggedUserSkills' },
  { tool: 'terminateEnrollment', purpose: 'This action is used to terminate an active enrollment.\n\ndependencyTools: getUserEnrollments' },
  { tool: 'triggerCandidateOnboarding', purpose: 'Triggers onboarding for existing candidates (no workflow). Use when the user asks to trigger onboarding for a candidate without mentioning workflows. Requires candidateIds (JSONArray of PKIDs from listOnboardingRecords) and formId (long, use the candidateFormId value returned by listOnboardingRecords when reportType=P_Candidate). Do NOT use this when workflows are also needed - call triggerWorkflow separately after.\n\ndependencyTools: listOnboardingRecords' },
  { tool: 'triggerEmployeeOnboarding', purpose: 'Triggers onboarding for existing employees (no workflow). Use when the user asks to trigger onboarding for an employee. Requires erecnoobj (JSONArray of employee erecnos - resolve via getEmployeeBasicDetails if needed). Does not trigger workflows.' },
  { tool: 'triggerWorkflow', purpose: 'Triggers the onboarding workflow for a candidate. Use when the user asks to initiate workflows for onboarding, independently of triggering the onboarding process itself. Requires candidateId (long) and isWFTrigger (boolean, always pass true). Do NOT combine with triggerCandidateOnboarding - each must be called independently.' },
  { tool: 'unAlignObjective', purpose: 'Removes alignment of an objective from its parent objective. Requires objectiveId (long).' },
  { tool: 'unpublishBenefitPlan', purpose: 'This action is used to unpublish a benefit plan removing it from employee visibility.\n\ndependencyTools: getBenefitPlans' },
  { tool: 'updateAbsentScheduler', purpose: 'Updates an absent scheduler by record_id (path). Partial PUT - omitted fields retain existing. TIME: same encoding as create. When applicable_for is sent, it fully replaces existing; for user applicability, use getEmployeeBasicDetails (searchErecNo). When notifications is sent, it replaces all rules. If notify_through_mail=1 (sent or already stored), notifications must be non-empty with day (1-10) and at least one action per entry. Resolve record_id via listAbsentSchedulers.\n\ndependencyTools: listAbsentSchedulers, getAbsentScheduler, getApplicableInfo, getEmployeeBasicDetails, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'updateAdditionalOptionsSettings', purpose: 'Updates attendance additional options settings. Supports partial updates - each flag is written independently.      DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show raw param names or JSON structures to the user.      Before calling:      1. Call getAdditionalOptionsSettings to fetch the current values.      After calling:      2. Call getAdditionalOptionsSettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAdditionalOptionsSettings' },
  { tool: 'updateAttendancePolicySettings', purpose: 'Updates the organization-wide default attendance policy (working hours, pay-period inclusion, late-night tracking, punch round-off, effective date). Supports partial updates.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=policy)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getAttendancePolicySettings to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getAttendancePolicySettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getAttendancePolicySettings, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails' },
  { tool: 'updateAttendanceSettingsMethods', purpose: 'Updates which attendance employee-request modules are enabled. Supports partial updates  -  omitted flags are preserved from the current configuration.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=methods)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getAttendanceSettingsMethods once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getAttendanceSettingsMethods' },
  { tool: 'updateBreak', purpose: 'Updates a break by record_id (path). Partial PUT. Duration: fixed break_time_in_mins OR accrual break_on_work_hrs. ACCRUAL FORMAT: break_on_work_hrs JSONArray tiers must use ONLY breakTime and workingHrs (int minutes). Example: [{breakTime:15,workingHrs:240}]. Do NOT use breakMinutes or working_hours - security rejects extra keys. WINDOW FORMAT: break_res_from_to_time uses ONLY fromTime and toTime. On auto-deduct fixed breaks do not change break_time_in_mins directly; update break_res_from_to_time or break_on_work_hrs. Resolve record_id via listBreaks; copy tier keys exactly from getBreak response.\n\ndependencyTools: listBreaks, getBreak, getShiftInfo' },
  { tool: 'updateBreakPolicySettings', purpose: 'Updates break policy configuration. Partial PUT - omitted fields retain existing values. Configurable: is_break_reg_enabled, is_add_break_enabled, is_edit_break_enabled, is_break_reg_reason_enabled, break_reg_reasons (comma-separated; replaces entire list), is_break_attachment_mandatory, break_reg_restricted_within (days), break_reg_allowed_count, break_reg_allowed_in_period (0=week, 1=month, 2=pay period), is_missed_brk_alert_enabled, notify flags, missed_brk_alert_users (erecno list), is_break_enabled, and missed-break exception toggles.\n\ndependencyTools: getBreakPolicySettings' },
  { tool: 'updateCheckinCheckoutSettings', purpose: 'Updates organization-wide check-in/check-out settings. Supports partial updates  -  omitted fields are prefilled. Not for working-hour FILO, minimum hours, or round-off  -  use updateAttendancePolicySettings instead. To disable a check-in/out reminder or deviation alert, send that minute param as -1 (not 0, not omission alone).         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=checkincheckout)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getCheckinCheckoutSettings to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getCheckinCheckoutSettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getCheckinCheckoutSettings' },
  { tool: 'updateDivision', purpose: 'Updates an existing division. Use getDivisions first to identify the correct division ID. All parameters are optional: \'name\' (updated display name, must be unique), \'description\' (updated description), \'zp_code\' (updated code, max 10 chars), \'parent_division\' (updated parent division ID for re-nesting). Returns the division\'s zoho_id on success.\n\ndependencyTools: getDivisions' },
  { tool: 'updateEntity', purpose: 'Updates an existing legal entity. Use getEntities first to identify the correct entity ID. All parameters are optional: \'name\' (updated display name, must be unique), \'description\' (updated description), \'zp_code\' (updated code, max 10 chars). Returns the entity\'s zoho_id on success.\n\ndependencyTools: getEntities' },
  { tool: 'updateKioskDevice', purpose: 'Updates a Kiosk device by device_id (path). Email is immutable. Optional: device_name, timezone, country_code, language_code, is_dynamic_punch_enabled, is_delete_captured_image_enabled. Resolve device_id via getKioskLoginUsers.\n\ndependencyTools: getKioskLoginUsers' },
  { tool: 'updateKioskDevicePassword', purpose: 'Changes a kiosk device\'s login password by device id (path). Required: old_password, new_password. Resolve the device id via getKioskLoginUsers.\n\ndependencyTools: getKioskLoginUsers' },
  { tool: 'updateLiveLocationTrackingSettings', purpose: 'Updates live location tracking settings. Supports partial updates - omitted fields are preserved from the current configuration. Two notification types are independent: (1) Location capture failure - GPS not received from employee device (is_notify_employee, is_notify_reporting_manager, is_notify_specific_users, specific_users, *_mail_template_id). (2) Out of geo range - GPS captured but outside geo-restricted area (is_notify_not_in_geo_employee, is_notify_not_in_geo_reporting_manager, is_notify_not_in_geo_specific_users, not_in_geo_specific_users, not_in_geo_*_mail_template_id). Do not mix type-1 params with type-2 scenarios.      DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show raw param names or JSON structures to the user.      Before calling:      1. Call getLiveLocationTrackingSettings to fetch the current values.      After calling:      2. Call getLiveLocationTrackingSettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getLiveLocationTrackingSettings' },
  { tool: 'updateOfficeInRemoteInSettings', purpose: 'Updates Office-In/Remote-In differentiation settings. Supports partial updates. For ip_ranges, send objects with index, fromIp, toIp; include id for existing ranges or omit id for new ones; always send the full ip_ranges list.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=officeinremotein)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getOfficeInRemoteInSettings to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getOfficeInRemoteInSettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getOfficeInRemoteInSettings, getKioskDeviceDetails, getGeoRangeDetails' },
  { tool: 'updateOnDutySettings', purpose: 'Updates on-duty configuration. Supports partial updates  -  omitted fields are prefilled. For od_types, send {id:name} format  -  existing IDs are edited, omitted IDs are deleted, key -1 adds a new type.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=onduty)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getOnDutySettings to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getOnDutySettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getOnDutySettings' },
  { tool: 'updatePermissionRule', purpose: 'Updates an existing hour-permission rule by permission_id (path). Partial PUT  -  omitted parameters keep existing values. For period_type: 1=weekly, 2=monthly.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=permission)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call listPermissionRules to resolve the rule by name, then getPermissionRule to fetch full current values. Never ask the user for a numeric permission_id  -  resolve it from the rule name.         After calling:         3. Call getPermissionRule once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, listPermissionRules, getPermissionRule, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'updatePresentByDefault', purpose: 'Updates a present-by-default group by record_id (path). Partial PUT - omitted fields retain existing values. Send to_date as empty to clear it. When applicable_for is sent, it fully replaces the existing applicability. Resolve record_id via listPresentByDefault.\n\ndependencyTools: listPresentByDefault, getPresentByDefault, getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'updateRecord', purpose: 'This action is used to update a record, and the recordId is mandatory. It starts by retrieving the formlinkname using the identifyForm tool, then obtains the recordId using the getRecords tool.      It fetches the field details using the getFields tool, based on the formId from identifyForm. The user\'s input is matched with the required fields, and the input is constructed using the RECORD_ADD_UPDATE PromptSection.      STRICT: For Lookup fields, call getLookupOptions with the relevant labelname values in the fields parameter. The response contains lookupOptions where each field labelname maps to an array of { Value, Id } objects. Match the user\'s text against Value and send the corresponding Id. NEVER send display strings for Lookup fields.      For Picklist and Dropdown fields, call getFieldOptions with the relevant labelname values to fetch available options. Match the user\'s input against the option values (case-sensitive). If an exact match is found, send the matched option value as-is. If no exact match is found, present the available options to the user and ask whether they want to choose from the existing options or quick-add the provided value as a new option.      STRICT: For Gender, BloodGroup and Country fields, call getFieldOptions with the relevant labelname values to fetch available options. The response contains an Options object where keys are internal identifiers and values are the display option texts (e.g., Options: {Option1: Male, Option2: Female, Option3: Others}). Match the user\'s input against the option values (case-sensitive). If an exact match is found, send the matched option value as-is. If no exact match is found, present the available options to the user and ask them to choose. NEVER send a value that is not present in the fetched options list.      If a Lookup Id cannot be resolved, ask the user to choose from available options or provide the ID instead of proceeding with a string value.      STRICT: For file or image fields, NEVER pass a raw chat fileId from `[Attached files: ...]`. First call useChatFileInField to bridge the chat file and obtain a new ZFS fileId; place that returned fileId in inputData for the file/image field AND set isFileId=true on this updateRecord call so the value is treated as a raw fileId instead of an encrypted token. If no file/image field is being assigned a fileId in this call, omit isFileId (default false).      EMPLOYEE STATUS CHANGE: When updating EmployeeStatus on the employee form to an inactive value and the employee has pending approvals, pass optional query param forward_to_erecno (erecno of the active employee who should receive forwarded approvals). Do NOT use forwardErecno on this API - that is the internal/web-only param name. If forward_to_erecno is omitted, a notification mail is sent and the status update proceeds. If forward_to_erecno is invalid (e.g. login-disabled user), validation fails on EmployeeStatus with an error code and message.      The final data is formatted as a string and passed as inputData, along with the mandatory recordId for the update operation.      POST-SUCCESS URL RULE (STRICT): After this call succeeds, MUST NOT emit ANY URL or \'View Your Record\' / \'Open <form> Record\' link to the just-updated record - there is no per-single-record view URL tool. Confirm success in plain language; optionally offer to open the records listing page and only call getRecordsViewUrl if the user confirms (use its returned URL verbatim). See OUTPUT_HYGIENE_GUARD rule 6.\n\ndependencyTools: identifyForm, getRecords, getFields, getFieldOptions, getLookupOptions' },
  { tool: 'updateRegularizationSettings', purpose: 'Updates regularization (attendance correction) configuration. Supports partial updates  -  omitted fields are prefilled.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=regularization)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getRegularizationSettings to fetch the current values.         After calling:         3. Call getRegularizationSettings once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getRegularizationSettings' },
  { tool: 'updateRemotePolicy', purpose: 'Updates an existing remote work policy by policy_id (path segment). Partial PUT  -  omitted fields are prefilled from the current policy. Key rule fields: type (1=employee raises request, 2=auto-approved), limit_restricted (if true: also provide days and period where 1=weekly/2=monthly), remote_approval_type (1=mandatory, 2=allow without approval for allowed days, 3=allow without approval + require request for excess), reason_mandatory, is_wfh_reason_enabled. When is_wfh_reason_enabled is true, wfh_reasons must include at least one non-empty reason.         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams (mode=remotepolicy)  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values or internal IDs.         2. Call getRemotePolicies to resolve the policy by name, then getRemotePolicy to fetch full current values. Never ask the user for a numeric policy_id  -  resolve it from the policy name.         After calling:         3. Call getRemotePolicy once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getRemotePolicies, getRemotePolicy, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getApplicableInfo' },
  { tool: 'updateReportSettings', purpose: 'Updates attendance report access settings. Partial PUT - omitted fields retain existing values. Configurable: is_report_view_allowed_to_manager, show_bal_ot_perm_to_user, show_bal_ot_perm_to_manager, edit_bal_ot_perm_to_user (requires show_bal_ot_perm_to_user), edit_bal_ot_perm_to_manager (requires show_bal_ot_perm_to_manager), is_carry_over_ot, is_payable_hrs_rep_view_allowed_to_manager, is_paid_brk_view_allowed_to_manager, is_un_paid_brk_view_allowed_to_manager.\n\ndependencyTools: getReportSettings' },
  { tool: 'updateSpecificPolicy', purpose: 'Updates a specific attendance policy identified by settings_id (path segment). Supports partial updates  -  omitted fields in any mode block are prefilled from the current policy via getData. To disable a check-in/out reminder or deviation alert, send that minute param as -1 (same rule as updateCheckinCheckoutSettings).         DISPLAY PRESENTATION: Do not show param names or JSON structures to the user.         Before calling:         1. Call getAttendanceSettingsParams with mode=specificpolicy  -  use returned label names when presenting any setting to the user. Never expose raw param_name values.         2. Call getSpecificPolicyDetail to fetch the current values.         Round-off vs Grace period (two completely separate features):         3. Round-off fields (early_check_in_round_off, late_check_in_round_off, early_check_out_round_off, late_check_out_round_off, and their *_mins variants)  -  adjusts the recorded punch time toward the shift boundary; it does NOT deduct leave. *_round_off=true snaps fully to the boundary; *_mins=N snaps only if within N minutes.         4. Grace period field (grace_period)  -  deducts leave when attendance violations exceed a configured frequency; it does NOT change the recorded punch time. grace_period is {rules:[{Intime, Outtime, Worktime, Coretime, allowDays, graceMode, period, redStat, leavetype}]}. Dimensions are determined by which time fields are present: Intime (late check-in), Outtime (early check-out), Worktime (work-hours deficit), Coretime (core-hours violation). Only add Worktime or Coretime if explicitly requested. period is int enum ONLY: 0=weekly, 1=monthly, 2=pay-period  -  NEVER a count of days; when user says "7 days" map to allowDays:7, not period:7. Never mix round-off with grace period  -  a late check-in tolerance goes inside a rule\'s Intime, not in late_check_in_mins.         After calling:         5. Call getSpecificPolicyDetail once to confirm the change was applied; report any discrepancy.\n\ndependencyTools: getAttendanceSettingsParams, getSpecificPolicies, getSpecificPolicyDetail, getDepartmentDetails, getLocationDetails, getShiftInfo, fetchLeaveTypes' },
  { tool: 'updateUnit', purpose: 'Updates an existing business unit. Use getUnits first to identify the correct unit ID. All parameters are optional: \'name\' (updated display name, must be unique), \'description\' (updated description), \'zp_code\' (updated code, max 10 chars). Returns the unit\'s zoho_id on success.\n\ndependencyTools: getUnits' },
  { tool: 'upgradeUserSkill', purpose: 'Upgrades a user\'s skill level. The skill_id parameter is required. Optionally provide upgradeReason (text up to 5000 chars) and a certification file. The URL contains the employee erecno as a dynamic path segment. Dependencies: [getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills]\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBasicDetails, getUserSkills' },
  { tool: 'uploadTimeAttendanceFile', purpose: 'Use when the user attaches a supporting file for a leave grant (or any leave-tracker request that needs supporting_document) before add/edit. Upload first, then pass the returned file_id and file_name in supporting_document on the grant/leave tool. Never invent file_id values.' },
  { tool: 'upsertKioskPortal', purpose: 'Creates the kiosk portal when none exists, otherwise renames it. Required: kiosk_name (letters and digits only; lowercased automatically). Call getKioskConfig first to check whether a kiosk portal already exists.\n\ndependencyTools: getKioskConfig' },
  { tool: 'viewCase', purpose: 'Use this tool to view the full details of a specific HR helpdesk case. Trigger phrases: \'view case\', \'view my case\', \'view helpdesk case\', \'show case details\', \'my case details\', \'case details\', \'open case\', \'get case info\', \'show my case\', \'case information\', \'view case id\'. DO NOT call identifyForm, allCaseslist, or any other tool for these. TWO scenarios: (A) If the user already provided a caseId number (e.g. 100002000000025015) - call this tool directly with that caseId. (B) If no caseId is provided - use dependency tools to get the user\'s case list, ask them to pick one, then call this tool with the chosen caseId.\n\ndependencyTools: listMyCases, listMyRequests' },
  { tool: 'viewCaseCategory', purpose: 'Use this tool to fetch full details of a specific HR helpdesk category, including its name, description, subcategory list, assigned agents, FAQs, and priority settings. Trigger phrases: \'show category details\', \'view category info\', \'what is this category about\', \'category description\', \'get category details\', \'show subcategories of a category\', \'fetch category details\'. Default to mode=\'userView\' for all regular users. Use mode=\'adminView\' ONLY when the user is confirmed to be an HR admin. TWO scenarios: (A) If the user already provided a categoryId - call this tool directly with that categoryId. (B) If categoryId is NOT known - use dependency tools to list all categories, ask the user to pick one, then call this tool with the chosen categoryId.\n\ndependencyTools: listAllCategory' },
  { tool: 'waiveEnrollment', purpose: 'Waives off from an enrolled benefit plan. Use when the employee wants to opt out of a plan they are enrolled in.      SELF USAGE: Use the current user\'s erecno when waiving their own enrollment.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: Resolve the target employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
  { tool: 'withdrawEnrollment', purpose: 'Withdraws from a requested plan enrollment that has not yet been finalized. Use when the user wants to cancel or withdraw a pending enrollment request.      SELF USAGE: Use the current user\'s erecno when withdrawing their own enrollment.      OTHER EMPLOYEE / ADMIN USAGE: Resolve the target employee\'s erecno using getEmployeeBasicDetails.\n\ndependencyTools: getEmployeeBenefitPlans, getEmployeeBasicDetails' },
];

